window.I7_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Robot Design & Parts 機器人設計與零件","cards":[{"w":"humanoid","p":"n.","d":"a robot that looks and moves like a person","c":"人形機器人","s":"The museum displayed a friendly humanoid that could walk and wave, so many children lined up to shake its hand.","t":"博物館展示了一個友善的人形機器人,它會走路和揮手,所以許多孩子排隊和它握手。"},{"w":"android","p":"n.","d":"a robot made to look very much like a human","c":"仿生人;擬真機器人","s":"In the film, the android looked so much like a real woman that nobody noticed, but her eyes sometimes glowed blue.","t":"在電影中,那個仿生人看起來非常像真正的女人,沒有人察覺,但她的眼睛有時會發出藍光。"},{"w":"cyborg","p":"n.","d":"a person whose body has machine parts added","c":"半機械人;生化人","s":"My brother loves science fiction stories about a cyborg with a metal arm, and he dreams of building one someday.","t":"我哥哥很喜歡關於一個裝著金屬手臂的半機械人的科幻故事,而且他夢想有一天能自己造一個。"},{"w":"manipulator","p":"n.","d":"a robot arm that picks up and moves objects","c":"機械手臂;操作臂","s":"The factory installed a new manipulator that lifts heavy car doors, so workers no longer hurt their backs on the job.","t":"工廠安裝了一支新的機械手臂來舉起沉重的車門,所以工人在工作時不再傷到背部。"},{"w":"gripper","p":"n.","d":"the part of a robot that holds things","c":"夾爪;抓取器","s":"The soft rubber gripper can pick up an egg without breaking it, and engineers are proud of this delicate design.","t":"這個柔軟的橡膠夾爪能拿起一顆蛋而不弄破,工程師們對這個精巧的設計感到自豪。"},{"w":"joint","p":"n.","d":"a place where two parts connect and can bend","c":"關節;接頭","s":"Each finger of the robot hand has three joint, so it can bend and hold a pen almost like a human hand.","t":"這隻機器手的每根手指都有三個關節,所以它能彎曲並幾乎像人手一樣握筆。"},{"w":"actuator","p":"n.","d":"a part that makes a machine move","c":"致動器;驅動器","s":"When the actuator in the robot's knee stopped working, the robot could not climb the stairs, so the team replaced it.","t":"當機器人膝蓋裡的致動器停止運作時,它就無法爬樓梯,所以團隊更換了它。"},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"a wheel with teeth that turns other wheels","c":"齒輪","s":"The old clock has many tiny gear inside, and they must turn together perfectly or the time will be wrong.","t":"這座老時鐘裡面有許多小齒輪,它們必須完美地一起轉動,否則時間就會不準。"},{"w":"lever","p":"n.","d":"a bar you push or pull to control a machine","c":"操縱桿;槓桿","s":"The driver pulled the lever to raise the robot's arm, but it moved too fast and almost hit the ceiling.","t":"駕駛員拉動操縱桿來升起機器人的手臂,但它移動得太快,差點撞到天花板。"},{"w":"hinge","p":"n.","d":"a metal part that lets a door or lid swing","c":"鉸鏈","s":"The robot's head moves on a strong hinge, so it can nod and look down at people who talk to it.","t":"機器人的頭靠一個堅固的鉸鏈轉動,所以它能點頭並低頭看著和它說話的人。"},{"w":"axle","p":"n.","d":"a rod that connects and turns two wheels","c":"車軸;輪軸","s":"The delivery robot stopped in the middle of the road because its front axle broke, and a technician had to fix it.","t":"送貨機器人停在路中間,因為它的前車軸斷了,技術人員必須去修理它。"},{"w":"pulley","p":"n.","d":"a wheel with a rope used to lift things","c":"滑輪","s":"Builders used a pulley to lift the heavy robot onto the stage, and the audience clapped when it arrived safely.","t":"工人用滑輪把沉重的機器人吊上舞台,當它安全抵達時觀眾都鼓掌了。"},{"w":"hydraulic","p":"adj.","d":"moved by liquid that is pushed through pipes","c":"液壓的","s":"The digger uses a hydraulic arm to lift tons of soil, so one machine can do the work of twenty people.","t":"這台挖土機使用液壓手臂來舉起好幾噸的土,所以一台機器就能做二十個人的工作。"},{"w":"pneumatic","p":"adj.","d":"powered by air that is pushed under pressure","c":"氣動的","s":"The robot hand has pneumatic muscles that fill with air, and this lets it hold soft fruit gently.","t":"這隻機器手有充氣的氣動肌肉,這讓它能輕柔地握住柔軟的水果。"},{"w":"wiring","p":"n.","d":"the system of wires inside a machine","c":"線路;配線","s":"After the flood, the wiring inside the robot was wet and damaged, so the engineers had to replace every cable.","t":"水災過後,機器人內部的線路又濕又受損,所以工程師必須更換每一條電線。"},{"w":"cable","p":"n.","d":"a thick wire that carries electricity or signals","c":"電纜;纜線","s":"Please do not step on the black cable on the floor, because it sends power to the robot on the stage.","t":"請不要踩到地上那條黑色的電纜,因為它正把電力傳送給舞台上的機器人。"},{"w":"microcontroller","p":"n.","d":"a very small computer that controls a device","c":"微控制器","s":"Our class programmed a cheap microcontroller to switch on a fan, and everyone cheered when the fan started spinning.","t":"我們班替一個便宜的微控制器寫程式來打開電風扇,當風扇開始轉動時大家都歡呼了。"},{"w":"lens","p":"n.","d":"curved glass that helps a camera see clearly","c":"鏡頭;透鏡","s":"The robot could not recognise faces because its camera lens was dirty, so I cleaned it with a soft cloth.","t":"機器人無法辨認臉孔,因為它的攝影機鏡頭髒了,所以我用軟布把它擦乾淨。"},{"w":"lidar","p":"n.","d":"a system that measures distance using laser light","c":"光達;雷射雷達","s":"Self-driving cars use lidar to measure how far away other cars are, and this helps them avoid accidents in traffic.","t":"自動駕駛汽車使用光達來測量其他車輛有多遠,這幫助它們在車流中避免事故。"},{"w":"infrared","p":"adj.","d":"using light that people cannot see but feel as heat","c":"紅外線的","s":"The security robot has an infrared camera, so it can see people in the dark when the lights are off.","t":"這台保全機器人有一台紅外線攝影機,所以在燈關掉時它也能在黑暗中看見人。"},{"w":"torque","p":"n.","d":"the turning force of an engine or motor","c":"扭力;轉矩","s":"This electric motor produces a lot of torque, so the small robot can push a heavy box across the floor.","t":"這個電動馬達產生很大的扭力,所以這台小機器人能把一個沉重的箱子推過地板。"},{"w":"lightweight","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy; easy to carry","c":"輕量的;重量輕的","s":"The new delivery drone is made from lightweight plastic, so it uses less battery and can fly much farther.","t":"新的送貨無人機是用輕量塑膠製成的,所以它耗電較少並且能飛得更遠。"},{"w":"alloy","p":"n.","d":"a metal made by mixing two or more metals","c":"合金","s":"The robot's body is made of a strong alloy, so it does not break when it falls down during tests.","t":"這台機器人的機身是用堅固的合金製成的,所以它在測試中跌倒時不會損壞。"},{"w":"titanium","p":"n.","d":"a strong, light, silver-coloured metal","c":"鈦","s":"Engineers chose titanium for the robot's legs because it is strong but light, although it is quite expensive.","t":"工程師為機器人的腿選擇了鈦,因為它堅固又輕,雖然它相當昂貴。"},{"w":"rechargeable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be filled with electricity again","c":"可充電的","s":"The toy robot runs on rechargeable batteries, so we just plug it in at night instead of buying new ones.","t":"這個玩具機器人使用可充電的電池,所以我們晚上只要插上電,而不用買新電池。"},{"w":"exoskeleton","p":"n.","d":"a wearable frame that gives the body extra strength","c":"外骨骼","s":"The nurse wears a light exoskeleton when she lifts patients, so her back no longer hurts at the end of the day.","t":"這位護理師在抬病人時會穿上輕型外骨骼,所以她一天結束時背部不再疼痛。"},{"w":"limb","p":"n.","d":"an arm or a leg","c":"肢體;四肢","s":"The robot dog lost one limb in the fall, but it could still walk slowly on its other three legs.","t":"那隻機器狗在跌倒時失去了一條腿,但它仍然能用另外三條腿慢慢走路。"},{"w":"payload","p":"n.","d":"the load that a vehicle or drone carries","c":"酬載;載重","s":"The drone can carry a payload of five kilograms, so farmers use it to spread seeds over their fields.","t":"這架無人機能攜帶五公斤的載重,所以農夫用它在田地上撒種子。"},{"w":"blueprint","p":"n.","d":"a detailed plan or drawing for building something","c":"藍圖;設計圖","s":"The students studied the blueprint of the robot carefully, and then they built every part exactly as shown.","t":"學生們仔細研究了機器人的設計圖,然後他們完全照著圖示製作每一個零件。"},{"w":"dismantle","p":"v.","d":"to take a machine apart into pieces","c":"拆解;拆卸","s":"We had to dismantle the broken robot to find the problem, but putting it back together took the whole afternoon.","t":"我們必須拆解這台壞掉的機器人來找出問題,但把它重新組裝回去花了整個下午。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Robots at Work: Factories & Logistics 工廠與物流中的機器人","cards":[{"w":"assembly line","p":"n.phr.","d":"a row of workers or machines that build products step by step","c":"裝配線;生產線","s":"Robots now do most of the welding on the car assembly line, while people check the finished cars for problems.","t":"機器人現在負責汽車裝配線上大部分的焊接工作,而人們則檢查完成的汽車是否有問題。"},{"w":"conveyor belt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a moving belt that carries things from place to place","c":"輸送帶","s":"Boxes move along the conveyor belt all day, and a robot arm picks out any box with the wrong label.","t":"箱子整天沿著輸送帶移動,而一支機器手臂會挑出任何貼錯標籤的箱子。"},{"w":"plant","p":"n.","d":"a large factory where things are made","c":"工廠;廠房","s":"The new battery plant near the city uses hundreds of robots, but it still employs about two thousand workers.","t":"城市附近的新電池工廠使用了數百台機器人,但它仍然僱用了大約兩千名員工。"},{"w":"mass production","p":"n.phr.","d":"making very large numbers of the same product","c":"大量生產","s":"mass production made cars cheaper in the twentieth century, and robots are making many products cheaper today.","t":"大量生產在二十世紀讓汽車變得更便宜,而機器人如今正讓許多產品變得更便宜。"},{"w":"industrial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with factories and making goods","c":"工業的","s":"Most industrial robots work behind safety fences, because their heavy arms move very fast and could injure people.","t":"大多數工業機器人在安全圍欄後面工作,因為它們沉重的手臂移動得很快,可能會傷到人。"},{"w":"forklift","p":"n.","d":"a small vehicle with two metal arms for lifting goods","c":"堆高機","s":"The driverless forklift carries boxes around the warehouse at night, so the shelves are full when staff arrive.","t":"這台無人駕駛的堆高機夜間在倉庫裡搬運箱子,所以員工到達時貨架已經補滿了。"},{"w":"pallet","p":"n.","d":"a flat wooden frame that goods are stacked on","c":"棧板;貨板","s":"The robot lifts each pallet of bottled water onto the truck, and it never drops a single bottle.","t":"機器人把每一個裝著瓶裝水的棧板抬上卡車,而且它從不掉落任何一瓶。"},{"w":"logistics","p":"n.","d":"organising how goods are stored and moved","c":"物流","s":"My cousin works in logistics for an online shop, and she says robots now pack most of the orders.","t":"我表姊在一家網路商店從事物流工作,她說現在大部分的訂單都是由機器人包裝的。"},{"w":"supply chain","p":"n.phr.","d":"all the steps from making a product to selling it","c":"供應鏈","s":"When the chip factory closed, the whole supply chain slowed down, so many shops had no new phones to sell.","t":"當晶片工廠關閉時,整個供應鏈都變慢了,所以許多商店沒有新手機可以賣。"},{"w":"parcel","p":"n.","d":"a package sent by post or delivery","c":"包裹","s":"A small robot brought the parcel to my door, and I picked it up after typing a code on its lid.","t":"一台小機器人把包裹送到我家門口,我在它的蓋子上輸入密碼後才拿到它。"},{"w":"dispatch","p":"v.","d":"to send something or someone somewhere","c":"派送;發送","s":"The system can dispatch a delivery robot within minutes, so customers often receive their lunch while it is still hot.","t":"這個系統能在幾分鐘內派出一台送貨機器人,所以顧客常常在午餐還熱的時候就收到。"},{"w":"courier","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that delivers packages","c":"快遞員;快遞公司","s":"The courier usually delivers our parcels by motorbike, but last week a drone dropped one in our garden.","t":"快遞員通常騎機車送我們的包裹,但上星期一架無人機把一個包裹丟在我們的花園裡。"},{"w":"loading dock","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where trucks are filled or emptied","c":"裝卸區;卸貨平台","s":"Robots carry the boxes to the loading dock, and then the drivers check them before the trucks leave.","t":"機器人把箱子搬到裝卸區,然後司機在卡車出發前檢查它們。"},{"w":"shelving","p":"n.","d":"a set of shelves for storing things","c":"貨架;架子","s":"The warehouse has tall metal shelving, and small robots climb up it to bring down the boxes people order.","t":"倉庫裡有高大的金屬貨架,小機器人會爬上去把人們訂購的箱子拿下來。"},{"w":"barcode","p":"n.","d":"a pattern of lines that a machine can read","c":"條碼","s":"Each box has a barcode on its side, so the robot knows exactly where to take it in the building.","t":"每個箱子側面都有一個條碼,所以機器人確切知道要把它送到大樓的哪裡。"},{"w":"scanner","p":"n.","d":"a machine that reads codes or makes pictures of things","c":"掃描器","s":"The scanner at the gate reads every package, and it beeps loudly if a box goes to the wrong area.","t":"門口的掃描器會讀取每個包裹,如果有箱子送錯區域,它就會大聲嗶嗶叫。"},{"w":"throughput","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work done in a period of time","c":"產能;處理量","s":"After the robots arrived, the factory's throughput doubled, but the managers still needed people to solve problems.","t":"機器人到來之後,工廠的產能翻倍了,但經理們仍然需要人來解決問題。"},{"w":"weld","p":"v.","d":"to join metal parts by melting them together","c":"焊接","s":"Robots can weld car parts faster than people, and they do not need to breathe the dangerous smoke.","t":"機器人能比人更快地焊接汽車零件,而且它們不需要吸入危險的煙霧。"},{"w":"welder","p":"n.","d":"a person or machine that joins metal by heating it","c":"焊接工;焊接機","s":"My uncle was a welder for twenty years, but now he trains young workers to use robot welding machines.","t":"我叔叔當了二十年的焊工,但現在他訓練年輕工人使用焊接機器人。"},{"w":"quality control","p":"n.phr.","d":"checking that products are made correctly","c":"品質管制;品管","s":"Cameras now help with quality control, because they can spot tiny scratches that tired workers might miss.","t":"攝影機現在協助品質管制,因為它們能發現疲倦的工人可能漏看的細小刮痕。"},{"w":"defect","p":"n.","d":"a fault or mistake in something that was made","c":"瑕疵;缺陷","s":"The camera found a small defect in the phone screen, so the robot removed it from the line immediately.","t":"攝影機在手機螢幕上發現一個小瑕疵,所以機器人立刻把它從生產線上移除。"},{"w":"defective","p":"adj.","d":"not made correctly; not working properly","c":"有瑕疵的;故障的","s":"The company called back thousands of defective toys, because a loose part could hurt young children.","t":"公司召回了數千個有瑕疵的玩具,因為一個鬆脫的零件可能會傷到幼童。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping machines in good condition","c":"維修;保養","s":"Robots do not get tired, but they need regular maintenance, so the factory stops them every Sunday for checks.","t":"機器人不會累,但它們需要定期保養,所以工廠每個星期天讓它們停機檢查。"},{"w":"repetitive","p":"adj.","d":"doing the same thing again and again","c":"重複的","s":"Robots are good at repetitive jobs like packing boxes, so workers can spend more time on creative tasks.","t":"機器人擅長像包裝箱子這樣重複的工作,所以工人能花更多時間在有創意的任務上。"},{"w":"heavy lifting","p":"n.phr.","d":"the work of picking up and moving heavy things","c":"搬運重物;粗重工作","s":"The robots do the heavy lifting in the warehouse, while staff focus on checking orders and helping customers.","t":"機器人在倉庫裡負責搬運重物,而員工則專注於檢查訂單和協助顧客。"},{"w":"operator","p":"n.","d":"a person who controls a machine","c":"操作員","s":"The crane operator watched the screen carefully, because one small mistake could drop the steel on the workers below.","t":"起重機操作員仔細地看著螢幕,因為一個小錯誤就可能把鋼材掉到下面的工人身上。"},{"w":"machinery","p":"n.","d":"machines in general, especially large ones","c":"機械;機器(總稱)","s":"Farmers in our village bought new machinery last year, so they can harvest rice with far fewer helpers.","t":"我們村子的農夫去年買了新機械,所以他們能用少得多的人手收割稻米。"},{"w":"cobot","p":"n.","d":"a robot designed to work safely next to people","c":"協作機器人","s":"The cobot works right beside the staff, and it stops at once if someone's hand comes too close.","t":"這台協作機器人就在員工旁邊工作,如果有人的手靠得太近,它會立刻停下來。"},{"w":"workstation","p":"n.","d":"the place where a worker or machine does a job","c":"工作站;工作台","s":"Each workstation on the line has one person and one robot, and they pass parts to each other all day.","t":"生產線上的每個工作站都有一個人和一台機器人,他們整天互相傳遞零件。"},{"w":"crane","p":"n.","d":"a tall machine for lifting very heavy objects","c":"起重機;吊車","s":"A huge crane lifted the containers off the ship, and it was controlled by a person in an office far away.","t":"一台巨大的起重機把貨櫃從船上吊起來,而它是由遠處辦公室裡的一個人控制的。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Service, Home & Medical Robots 服務、家用與醫療機器人","cards":[{"w":"robot vacuum","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small machine that cleans floors by itself","c":"掃地機器人","s":"Our robot vacuum cleans the living room while we are at work, but it often gets stuck under the sofa.","t":"我們的掃地機器人在我們上班時打掃客廳,但它常常卡在沙發底下。"},{"w":"lawnmower","p":"n.","d":"a machine for cutting grass","c":"割草機","s":"My neighbour bought a robot lawnmower that cuts the grass every morning, so his garden always looks tidy.","t":"我的鄰居買了一台機器人割草機,每天早上割草,所以他的花園總是看起來很整齊。"},{"w":"dishwasher","p":"n.","d":"a machine that washes plates and cups","c":"洗碗機","s":"We load the dishwasher after dinner, and the clean plates are ready before we go to bed.","t":"我們晚餐後把碗盤放進洗碗機,睡覺前乾淨的盤子就準備好了。"},{"w":"appliance","p":"n.","d":"a machine used in the home, like a fridge","c":"家電;家用電器","s":"Many new kitchen appliance can connect to the internet, so you can start the rice cooker from your phone.","t":"許多新的廚房家電可以連上網路,所以你可以用手機啟動電鍋。"},{"w":"smart home","p":"n.phr.","d":"a house where devices are controlled by the internet","c":"智慧家庭;智慧住宅","s":"In our smart home, the lights turn on when we walk in, and the heater starts before we wake up.","t":"在我們的智慧家庭裡,我們一走進去燈就會亮,而暖氣在我們起床前就開始運作。"},{"w":"voice command","p":"n.phr.","d":"a spoken order that a machine follows","c":"語音指令","s":"Grandpa uses a voice command to turn on the TV, because the small buttons on the remote are hard to see.","t":"爺爺用語音指令打開電視,因為遙控器上的小按鈕很難看清楚。"},{"w":"vending machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that sells drinks or snacks","c":"自動販賣機","s":"The vending machine at the station takes phone payments, so I bought a drink without any coins.","t":"車站的自動販賣機接受手機付款,所以我沒用任何硬幣就買了一杯飲料。"},{"w":"self-checkout","p":"n.","d":"a machine where shoppers pay without a cashier","c":"自助結帳機","s":"The supermarket added six self-checkout machines, but older customers still prefer to queue for a person.","t":"超市增加了六台自助結帳機,但年長的顧客仍然比較喜歡排隊找人結帳。"},{"w":"kiosk","p":"n.","d":"a small screen or booth where you order or buy things","c":"自助點餐機;服務亭","s":"I ordered my burger at the touchscreen kiosk, and a robot brought it to my table ten minutes later.","t":"我在觸控自助點餐機點了漢堡,十分鐘後一台機器人把它送到我的桌上。"},{"w":"cashier","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes money in a shop","c":"收銀員","s":"The friendly cashier at the corner shop knows all the customers, so people still visit even though machines are faster.","t":"街角商店那位友善的收銀員認識所有顧客,所以即使機器比較快,人們仍然會去光顧。"},{"w":"receptionist","p":"n.","d":"a person who greets visitors at a front desk","c":"接待員;櫃台人員","s":"The hotel replaced its night receptionist with a talking robot, but guests complained that it could not answer simple questions.","t":"飯店用一台會說話的機器人取代了夜班接待員,但客人抱怨它無法回答簡單的問題。"},{"w":"waiter","p":"n.","d":"a person who serves food in a restaurant","c":"服務生","s":"The restaurant uses a robot waiter to carry dishes, while the staff spend more time chatting with customers.","t":"這家餐廳使用機器人服務生送菜,而員工則花更多時間和顧客聊天。"},{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a small, regular job in the house","c":"家事;雜務","s":"Washing clothes used to be a hard chore, but now machines do most of the work for us.","t":"洗衣服以前是一件辛苦的家事,但現在機器幫我們做了大部分的工作。"},{"w":"errand","p":"n.","d":"a short trip to buy or deliver something","c":"跑腿;差事","s":"My mother asked a delivery robot to do a quick errand, so it brought medicine from the pharmacy next door.","t":"我媽媽請一台送貨機器人去跑腿,於是它從隔壁藥局送來了藥。"},{"w":"mop","p":"v.","d":"to clean a floor with a wet cloth on a stick","c":"拖(地)","s":"This robot can vacuum and mop the floor at the same time, so our kitchen stays clean every day.","t":"這台機器人能同時吸塵和拖地,所以我們的廚房每天都保持乾淨。"},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"the business of hotels, restaurants and serving guests","c":"餐旅業;款待","s":"Robots are becoming common in the hospitality industry, but many travellers still want a warm smile from a real person.","t":"機器人在餐旅業越來越常見,但許多旅客仍然希望得到真人溫暖的微笑。"},{"w":"greet","p":"v.","d":"to say hello to someone when they arrive","c":"迎接;打招呼","s":"A small robot at the bank door will greet you by name, and then it tells you which counter to visit.","t":"銀行門口的小機器人會叫著你的名字跟你打招呼,然後告訴你要去哪個櫃台。"},{"w":"social robot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a robot designed to talk and interact with people","c":"社交機器人","s":"The social robot in the care home tells jokes and plays games, so the residents feel less bored in the afternoon.","t":"安養院裡的社交機器人會講笑話和玩遊戲,所以住民下午比較不會無聊。"},{"w":"surgical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with medical operations","c":"外科的;手術的","s":"The hospital bought a surgical robot that can make very small cuts, so patients recover faster after their operations.","t":"醫院買了一台能做出非常小切口的手術機器人,所以病人手術後恢復得更快。"},{"w":"surgeon","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who performs operations","c":"外科醫生","s":"The surgeon controlled the robot from a screen beside the bed, and the operation finished an hour early.","t":"外科醫生從病床旁的螢幕控制機器人,而手術提早了一個小時完成。"},{"w":"incision","p":"n.","d":"a cut made into the body during an operation","c":"切口","s":"The robot made a tiny incision in my father's side, so he could walk around the next day.","t":"機器人在我爸爸的側腹做了一個很小的切口,所以他隔天就能四處走動。"},{"w":"keyhole surgery","p":"n.phr.","d":"an operation done through very small cuts","c":"微創手術;內視鏡手術","s":"My aunt had keyhole surgery on her knee, and she was back at work in less than two weeks.","t":"我阿姨的膝蓋做了微創手術,不到兩週她就回去上班了。"},{"w":"prosthetic","p":"adj.","d":"artificial and used to replace a missing body part","c":"義肢的;假體的","s":"The runner lost her leg in an accident, but with a prosthetic leg she now competes in international races.","t":"這位跑者在意外中失去了一條腿,但靠著義肢腿,她現在參加國際比賽。"},{"w":"carer","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after someone who is ill or old","c":"照顧者;看護","s":"Robots can remind patients to take medicine, but they cannot replace a kind carer who listens and understands.","t":"機器人能提醒病人吃藥,但它們無法取代一位會傾聽和理解的親切照顧者。"},{"w":"care home","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where old people live and are looked after","c":"安養院;養護中心","s":"The care home has a robot that delivers meals to each room, so the nurses have more time to talk with residents.","t":"這家安養院有一台把餐點送到每個房間的機器人,所以護理師有更多時間和住民聊天。"},{"w":"ward","p":"n.","d":"a large room in a hospital for several patients","c":"病房","s":"A robot moves through the children's ward at night, and it checks each child's temperature without waking them up.","t":"一台機器人夜間在兒童病房裡移動,它會在不吵醒孩子的情況下量每個孩子的體溫。"},{"w":"disinfect","p":"v.","d":"to clean something to kill germs","c":"消毒","s":"The hospital uses robots with strong lights to disinfect the rooms, so nurses are less likely to catch infections.","t":"醫院使用帶有強光的機器人來消毒房間,所以護理師比較不容易被感染。"},{"w":"dispense","p":"v.","d":"to give out medicine or other things","c":"配(藥);分發","s":"The machine can dispense the right pills for each patient, and it keeps a record so nurses can check later.","t":"這台機器能為每位病人配發正確的藥丸,並且會保存紀錄讓護理師之後檢查。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Control & Programming 控制與程式設計","cards":[{"w":"reprogram","p":"v.","d":"to give a machine new instructions","c":"重新設定程式","s":"The engineers had to reprogram the robot after the factory changed its products, but the job took only one day.","t":"工廠更換產品後,工程師必須重新設定機器人的程式,但這份工作只花了一天。"},{"w":"operating system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main software that runs a computer or robot","c":"作業系統","s":"The robot's operating system needed an update, so it restarted by itself in the middle of the night.","t":"機器人的作業系統需要更新,所以它在半夜自己重新啟動了。"},{"w":"remote-controlled","p":"adj.","d":"controlled from a distance using radio signals","c":"遙控的","s":"My little brother got a remote-controlled car for his birthday, and he drove it around the kitchen all afternoon.","t":"我弟弟生日時得到一台遙控車,他整個下午都在廚房裡開著它到處跑。"},{"w":"joystick","p":"n.","d":"a stick you move to control a machine or game","c":"搖桿;操縱桿","s":"The pilot moved the joystick gently to the left, and the underwater robot turned towards the shipwreck.","t":"操作員輕輕地把搖桿往左推,水下機器人就轉向了沉船。"},{"w":"touchscreen","p":"n.","d":"a screen you control by touching it","c":"觸控螢幕","s":"Workers tell the robot what to do on a large touchscreen, so they do not need to learn any computer language.","t":"工人在一個大型觸控螢幕上告訴機器人要做什麼,所以他們不需要學任何電腦語言。"},{"w":"real-time","p":"adj.","d":"happening immediately, with no delay","c":"即時的","s":"The drone sends real-time video to the firefighters, so they can see where people are trapped inside the building.","t":"無人機把即時影像傳給消防員,所以他們能看到人們被困在建築物的哪裡。"},{"w":"computer vision","p":"n.phr.","d":"technology that lets computers understand images","c":"電腦視覺","s":"Thanks to computer vision, the robot can tell ripe tomatoes from green ones, so it picks only the ready fruit.","t":"多虧了電腦視覺,機器人能分辨成熟和未熟的番茄,所以它只採摘成熟的果實。"},{"w":"deep learning","p":"n.phr.","d":"a kind of AI that learns from huge amounts of examples","c":"深度學習","s":"The robot improved its walking through deep learning, and after thousands of tries it stopped falling over.","t":"這台機器人透過深度學習改善了走路的能力,在嘗試數千次之後它不再跌倒了。"},{"w":"self-learning","p":"adj.","d":"able to improve by itself without new instructions","c":"自我學習的","s":"The self-learning vacuum remembers where the furniture is, so it cleans our flat faster every week.","t":"這台能自我學習的吸塵器記得家具的位置,所以它每週打掃我們公寓的速度都更快。"},{"w":"calibrate","p":"v.","d":"to adjust a machine so that it measures correctly","c":"校準;校正","s":"We must calibrate the robot's camera every month, or it starts to put the parts in slightly the wrong place.","t":"我們每個月都必須校準機器人的攝影機,否則它會開始把零件放在稍微錯誤的位置。"},{"w":"troubleshoot","p":"v.","d":"to find and fix problems in a machine or system","c":"排除故障;檢修","s":"When the robot stopped moving, the technician tried to troubleshoot the problem, but she finally called the company for help.","t":"當機器人停止移動時,技術人員試著排除故障,但她最後還是打電話向公司求助。"},{"w":"debug","p":"v.","d":"to find and remove mistakes in computer code","c":"除錯","s":"Our team spent all night trying to debug the program, because the robot kept turning left instead of right.","t":"我們的隊伍整晚都在試著替程式除錯,因為機器人一直向左轉而不是向右轉。"},{"w":"reboot","p":"v.","d":"to turn a computer or machine off and on again","c":"重新開機","s":"If the robot freezes, just reboot it by holding the red button, and it usually works again in a minute.","t":"如果機器人當機,只要按住紅色按鈕將它重新開機,通常一分鐘後就能恢復運作。"},{"w":"override","p":"v.","d":"to take control and cancel what a machine is doing","c":"手動接管;推翻(決定)","s":"The driver can override the self-driving system at any time, so she grabbed the wheel when a child ran into the road.","t":"駕駛隨時可以手動接管自動駕駛系統,所以當一個孩子衝到馬路上時她立刻抓住方向盤。"},{"w":"emergency stop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a button that turns a machine off immediately","c":"緊急停止(按鈕)","s":"Every robot in the factory has a big red emergency stop button, and workers practise using it once a month.","t":"工廠裡的每台機器人都有一個紅色大緊急停止按鈕,工人每個月練習使用一次。"},{"w":"fail-safe","p":"adj.","d":"designed to stay safe if something goes wrong","c":"故障安全的;萬無一失的","s":"The lift has a fail-safe brake, so it will not fall even if the power suddenly goes off.","t":"這部電梯有故障安全煞車,所以即使突然停電,它也不會掉下去。"},{"w":"crash","p":"v.","d":"(of a computer) to stop working suddenly","c":"當機;(電腦)崩潰","s":"The computer system crash during the busy holiday season, so the robots stopped and hundreds of orders were late.","t":"電腦系統在忙碌的假期期間當機了,所以機器人停了下來,數百筆訂單都延誤了。"},{"w":"freeze","p":"v.","d":"(of a screen or machine) to stop moving or responding","c":"當住;凍結","s":"The robot's screen froze in the middle of the demonstration, so the presenter laughed and told a joke instead.","t":"示範到一半時機器人的螢幕當住了,所以主持人笑了笑並改講一個笑話。"},{"w":"wireless","p":"adj.","d":"working without wires, using radio signals","c":"無線的","s":"The robots talk to each other through a wireless network, so there are no cables lying on the factory floor.","t":"機器人透過無線網路互相溝通,所以工廠地板上沒有電線散落。"},{"w":"tablet","p":"n.","d":"a small flat computer with a touchscreen","c":"平板電腦","s":"The farmer checks his robot tractors on a tablet, so he can watch them while he drinks his morning tea.","t":"這位農夫用平板電腦查看他的機器人拖拉機,所以他能一邊喝早茶一邊看著它們。"},{"w":"engineer","p":"n.","d":"a person who designs and builds machines","c":"工程師","s":"My sister wants to become an engineer who designs robots for hospitals, so she studies maths and physics very hard.","t":"我姊姊想成為設計醫院用機器人的工程師,所以她非常努力地學習數學和物理。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"operated by machinery; connected with machines","c":"機械的","s":"The old robot made loud mechanical noises when it moved, but the new model is almost completely silent.","t":"舊型機器人移動時會發出很大的機械噪音,但新型號幾乎完全安靜。"},{"w":"electronic","p":"adj.","d":"using small electrical parts like chips","c":"電子的","s":"Old electronic devices should be recycled properly, because they contain metals that can harm the environment.","t":"舊的電子裝置應該妥善回收,因為它們含有會危害環境的金屬。"},{"w":"technician","p":"n.","d":"a skilled worker who repairs or looks after machines","c":"技術人員;技師","s":"A technician visits the hotel every week to check the robots, and she also teaches the staff how to fix small problems.","t":"一位技術人員每週到飯店檢查機器人,她也教員工如何修理小問題。"},{"w":"mechatronics","p":"n.","d":"the study that combines machines, electronics and computing","c":"機電整合","s":"My cousin is studying mechatronics at university, and he hopes to build farming robots after he graduates.","t":"我表哥在大學就讀機電整合,他希望畢業後能製造農業機器人。"},{"w":"GPS","p":"n.","d":"a system that uses satellites to show your location","c":"全球定位系統","s":"The lawnmower uses GPS to stay inside the garden, so it never wanders onto the road.","t":"這台割草機使用全球定位系統來保持在花園範圍內,所以它從不會跑到馬路上。"},{"w":"mapping","p":"n.","d":"making a map or plan of an area","c":"製圖;建立地圖","s":"The robot vacuum starts by mapping every room, and then it plans the fastest way to clean the house.","t":"掃地機器人一開始會替每個房間建立地圖,然後規劃打掃房子最快的路線。"},{"w":"autopilot","p":"n.","d":"a system that flies a plane or drives a car automatically","c":"自動駕駛(系統)","s":"The plane flew on autopilot for most of the journey, but the pilots landed it themselves because of strong winds.","t":"這架飛機大部分航程都以自動駕駛飛行,但因為強風,飛行員親自讓它降落。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Robots in Sport & Officiating 運動中的機器人與裁判科技","cards":[{"w":"umpire","p":"n.","d":"an official who makes decisions in tennis, cricket or baseball","c":"裁判(網球、棒球等)","s":"The league is testing a robot umpire that calls balls and strikes, but some players say it takes the fun out of baseball.","t":"聯盟正在測試一位判定好壞球的機器人裁判,但有些球員說這讓棒球失去了樂趣。"},{"w":"referee","p":"n.","d":"an official who controls a football or basketball game","c":"裁判(足球、籃球等)","s":"The referee checked the video screen before giving the goal, so the angry fans finally calmed down.","t":"裁判在判定進球之前先查看了影像螢幕,所以憤怒的球迷終於冷靜下來。"},{"w":"line judge","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official who decides if a ball is in or out","c":"司線員;邊線裁判","s":"Many tennis tournaments no longer use a line judge, because electronic cameras can call the lines more accurately.","t":"許多網球賽不再使用司線員,因為電子攝影機能更精準地判定界線。"},{"w":"officiate","p":"v.","d":"to act as the official in charge of a game","c":"擔任裁判;主持","s":"My uncle used to officiate local football matches, but now he says the video system makes the job very different.","t":"我叔叔以前常擔任地方足球賽的裁判,但他現在說影像系統讓這份工作變得很不一樣。"},{"w":"ruling","p":"n.","d":"an official decision","c":"裁決;判決","s":"The player was unhappy with the ruling, but he accepted it after the replay showed the ball was out.","t":"這位球員對裁決不滿,但在重播顯示球出界後他接受了。"},{"w":"overturn","p":"v.","d":"to officially change a decision","c":"推翻;撤銷(判決)","s":"The video referee decided to overturn the penalty, because the replay showed that the defender never touched the striker.","t":"影像裁判決定推翻這個罰球判決,因為重播顯示防守球員從未碰到前鋒。"},{"w":"replay","p":"n.","d":"a recording of part of a game shown again","c":"重播","s":"The replay showed that the runner was safe, so the umpire changed his call and the crowd cheered.","t":"重播顯示跑者是安全上壘,所以裁判改變了判決,觀眾都歡呼起來。"},{"w":"slow motion","p":"n.phr.","d":"showing a video more slowly than real speed","c":"慢動作","s":"In slow motion, you can see the ball just touch the line, but it was impossible to see with the eye.","t":"在慢動作中,你能看到球剛好碰到線,但用肉眼是不可能看清楚的。"},{"w":"goal-line technology","p":"n.phr.","d":"cameras that show whether a ball crossed the goal line","c":"門線技術","s":"goal-line technology tells the referee within one second whether the ball went in, so there are fewer arguments after big matches.","t":"門線技術在一秒內告訴裁判球是否進門,所以大比賽後的爭議少了很多。"},{"w":"offside","p":"adj.","d":"in a position on the field that breaks the rules","c":"越位的","s":"The striker was offside by only a few centimetres, but the computer lines showed it clearly and the goal was cancelled.","t":"這名前鋒只越位了幾公分,但電腦畫線清楚地顯示出來,所以進球被取消了。"},{"w":"foul","p":"n.","d":"an action that breaks the rules of a game","c":"犯規","s":"The referee missed the foul at first, but the video assistant told him to look at the screen again.","t":"裁判一開始漏看了這次犯規,但影像助理請他再看一次螢幕。"},{"w":"strike zone","p":"n.phr.","d":"the area over home plate where a pitch counts as a strike","c":"好球帶","s":"Every batter has a slightly different strike zone, so the robot umpire must measure each player's height.","t":"每位打者的好球帶都略有不同,所以機器人裁判必須測量每位球員的身高。"},{"w":"pitcher","p":"n.","d":"the baseball player who throws the ball to the batter","c":"投手","s":"The pitcher threw the ball very fast, and the robot umpire called it a strike before the crowd could even see it.","t":"投手把球投得非常快,觀眾還沒看清楚,機器人裁判就判定是好球了。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"the baseball player who tries to hit the ball","c":"打者","s":"The batter argued that the ball was too low, but the computer showed it had touched the edge of the zone.","t":"打者爭辯說那球太低,但電腦顯示它碰到了好球帶的邊緣。"},{"w":"court","p":"n.","d":"an area marked for playing tennis or basketball","c":"球場(網球、籃球等)","s":"Cameras around the tennis court track the ball at high speed, so players can challenge any call they disagree with.","t":"網球場周圍的攝影機高速追蹤球,所以球員可以對任何不同意的判決提出挑戰。"},{"w":"rally","p":"n.","d":"a long series of hits in tennis or badminton","c":"(網球等)來回對打","s":"The two players had a forty-shot rally, and the crowd stood up to clap when it finally ended.","t":"兩位選手進行了四十拍的來回對打,當它終於結束時,觀眾都站起來鼓掌。"},{"w":"spectator","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches a sports event","c":"觀眾","s":"Every spectator in the stadium could see the replay on the big screen, so nobody doubted the referee's final decision.","t":"體育場裡的每一位觀眾都能在大螢幕上看到重播,所以沒有人懷疑裁判的最後決定。"},{"w":"stadium","p":"n.","d":"a large sports ground with seats around it","c":"體育場","s":"The new stadium has robots that deliver snacks to fans' seats, so nobody misses the action while queuing.","t":"新的體育場有把點心送到球迷座位的機器人,所以沒有人會因為排隊而錯過精彩畫面。"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a sports competition with many games or rounds","c":"錦標賽;聯賽","s":"The robot football tournament attracted teams from twenty countries, and our school's team reached the final round.","t":"機器人足球錦標賽吸引了來自二十個國家的隊伍,而我們學校的隊伍打進了決賽。"},{"w":"league","p":"n.","d":"a group of teams that play against each other","c":"聯盟","s":"The baseball league plans to use electronic umpires next season, but the players' union wants more tests first.","t":"棒球聯盟計畫下一季使用電子裁判,但球員工會希望先做更多測試。"},{"w":"athlete","p":"n.","d":"a person who is good at sports and trains hard","c":"運動員","s":"Wearable sensors tell each athlete how fast they are running, so coaches can plan better training sessions.","t":"穿戴式感測器告訴每位運動員他們跑得多快,所以教練能規劃更好的訓練課程。"},{"w":"coach","p":"n.","d":"a person who trains a sports team or player","c":"教練","s":"Our coach uses video software to study every match, and she shows us exactly where we made mistakes.","t":"我們的教練使用影像軟體研究每一場比賽,她會清楚地告訴我們哪裡犯了錯。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"the person or team you play against","c":"對手","s":"The table tennis robot is a tireless opponent, so players can practise for hours without needing a partner.","t":"這台桌球機器人是一個永不疲倦的對手,所以選手能練習好幾個小時而不需要搭檔。"},{"w":"scoreboard","p":"n.","d":"a large board showing the score of a game","c":"記分板","s":"The scoreboard showed the speed of every serve, and the fans cheered when it reached two hundred kilometres per hour.","t":"記分板顯示每一次發球的速度,當它達到每小時兩百公里時球迷都歡呼了。"},{"w":"tiebreak","p":"n.","d":"an extra game played to decide a winner when scores are equal","c":"搶七;決勝局","s":"The match went to a tiebreak, and one close line call decided who would win the whole tournament.","t":"這場比賽進入了搶七,而一個接近邊線的判決決定了誰會贏得整個錦標賽。"},{"w":"analytics","p":"n.","d":"the study of data to find useful patterns","c":"數據分析","s":"Teams now use analytics to choose players, but some fans think numbers cannot measure a player's heart.","t":"球隊現在用數據分析來挑選球員,但有些球迷認為數字無法衡量一位球員的鬥志。"},{"w":"motion capture","p":"n.phr.","d":"recording body movements with sensors to study them","c":"動作捕捉","s":"The golfer trained with motion capture, so she could see on a screen exactly how her body moved during each swing.","t":"這位高爾夫球員使用動作捕捉訓練,所以她能在螢幕上清楚看到每次揮桿時身體如何移動。"},{"w":"esports","p":"n.","d":"competitive video gaming watched by audiences","c":"電子競技","s":"My cousin plays esports professionally, and millions of fans watch his matches online every weekend.","t":"我表哥以職業身分打電子競技,每個週末有數百萬名粉絲在網路上觀看他的比賽。"},{"w":"championship","p":"n.","d":"a competition to find the best player or team","c":"冠軍賽;錦標賽","s":"The robot dance championship was held in Taipei this year, and teams spent months preparing their routines.","t":"機器人舞蹈錦標賽今年在台北舉行,各隊花了好幾個月準備他們的表演。"},{"w":"sportsmanship","p":"n.","d":"fair and polite behaviour when playing sports","c":"運動家精神","s":"The young player showed great sportsmanship when he admitted the ball was out, although the camera had not seen it.","t":"這位年輕選手承認球出界了,展現了很好的運動家精神,雖然攝影機並沒有拍到。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Jobs, Economy & the Future of Work 工作、經濟與未來職場","cards":[{"w":"blue-collar","p":"adj.","d":"doing physical work, often in factories or building","c":"藍領的;勞力工作的","s":"Many blue-collar workers worry about robots, but plumbers and electricians are still in high demand.","t":"許多藍領工人擔心機器人,但水電工和電工的需求仍然很高。"},{"w":"white-collar","p":"adj.","d":"doing office work rather than physical work","c":"白領的;辦公室工作的","s":"People once believed robots would only take factory jobs, but now AI is changing white-collar jobs like accounting too.","t":"人們曾經認為機器人只會搶走工廠工作,但現在人工智慧也在改變像會計這樣的白領工作。"},{"w":"unskilled","p":"adj.","d":"not having special training for a job","c":"非技術性的;無專業技能的","s":"Robots have replaced many unskilled jobs in warehouses, so the government offers free training courses for those workers.","t":"機器人已經取代了倉庫裡許多非技術性的工作,所以政府為那些工人提供免費的訓練課程。"},{"w":"skilled","p":"adj.","d":"having the training to do a job well","c":"有技術的;熟練的","s":"The company needs skilled workers who can repair robots, but it is hard to find enough of them.","t":"公司需要能修理機器人的有技術的工人,但很難找到足夠的人手。"},{"w":"labourer","p":"n.","d":"a person who does hard physical work","c":"勞工;體力勞動者","s":"My grandfather worked as a labourer on building sites, and he says machines now do the hardest lifting.","t":"我祖父以前在工地當勞工,他說機器現在負責最吃力的搬運工作。"},{"w":"job loss","p":"n.phr.","d":"when people lose their jobs","c":"失業;工作流失","s":"The new robots led to some job loss at the factory, but the company also hired fifty technicians.","t":"新機器人導致工廠出現了一些工作流失,但公司也僱用了五十名技術人員。"},{"w":"redeploy","p":"v.","d":"to move workers to a different job or place","c":"重新調派;調職","s":"Instead of firing staff, the bank decided to redeploy them to customer service after the machines took over counting cash.","t":"機器接手點鈔工作後,銀行決定不解僱員工,而是把他們調派到客戶服務部門。"},{"w":"reskill","p":"v.","d":"to learn new skills for a different job","c":"再培訓;學習新技能","s":"Many cashiers chose to reskill as computer helpers, and the company paid for their evening classes.","t":"許多收銀員選擇學習新技能轉當電腦助理,而公司替他們支付了夜間課程的費用。"},{"w":"workplace","p":"n.","d":"the place where people do their jobs","c":"工作場所;職場","s":"Robots have made the workplace much safer, because they now handle the dangerous chemicals instead of people.","t":"機器人讓工作場所安全了許多,因為現在由它們而不是人來處理危險的化學品。"},{"w":"colleague","p":"n.","d":"a person you work with","c":"同事","s":"My colleague was nervous about the new robot at first, but now she says it is the best helper she has ever had.","t":"我的同事一開始對新機器人很緊張,但她現在說那是她遇過最好的幫手。"},{"w":"manpower","p":"n.","d":"the number of workers available for a job","c":"人力","s":"The farm lacked manpower during the harvest, so the owner rented a fruit-picking robot for two months.","t":"農場在收成期間缺乏人力,所以農場主人租了一台採果機器人兩個月。"},{"w":"headcount","p":"n.","d":"the total number of people employed","c":"員工人數","s":"The company reduced its headcount after it bought robots, but it promised that no one would lose their job suddenly.","t":"公司購買機器人後減少了員工人數,但它承諾不會有人突然失去工作。"},{"w":"payroll","p":"n.","d":"the list of workers a company pays, or the money paid","c":"薪資名冊;薪資總額","s":"The factory's payroll has fallen since the robots arrived, so the owners have more money to spend on research.","t":"自從機器人到來後,工廠的薪資總額下降了,所以老闆有更多錢可以花在研發上。"},{"w":"overtime","p":"n.","d":"extra hours worked after the normal working day","c":"加班","s":"Before the robots came, workers often did overtime at night, but now most of them go home at five o'clock.","t":"在機器人來之前,工人常常在晚上加班,但現在大部分的人五點就回家了。"},{"w":"part-time","p":"adj.","d":"working only some hours of the day or week","c":"兼職的","s":"She took a part-time job at the robot café while studying, and she learned how to fix the coffee machine.","t":"她在求學期間在機器人咖啡館找了一份兼職工作,而且學會了如何修理咖啡機。"},{"w":"pension","p":"n.","d":"money paid regularly to people after they stop working","c":"退休金;養老金","s":"Some economists suggest a tax on robots to pay for pension, because there will be fewer young workers in the future.","t":"一些經濟學家建議對機器人課稅來支付退休金,因為未來的年輕勞工會變少。"},{"w":"robot tax","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tax on companies that use robots instead of workers","c":"機器人稅","s":"Supporters say a robot tax could pay for training courses, but business leaders argue that it would slow down progress.","t":"支持者說機器人稅可以支付訓練課程的費用,但企業領袖認為那會拖慢進步。"},{"w":"competitor","p":"n.","d":"a company that tries to sell more than another","c":"競爭對手","s":"Our competitor started using delivery drones last year, so our company had to find a faster way to send parcels.","t":"我們的競爭對手去年開始使用送貨無人機,所以我們公司必須找到更快寄送包裹的方法。"},{"w":"market share","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of total sales a company has","c":"市占率","s":"The company gained market share after it lowered prices, because its new robots made production much cheaper.","t":"公司降價後獲得了更多市占率,因為它的新機器人讓生產成本便宜了許多。"},{"w":"economies of scale","p":"n.phr.","d":"lower costs per item when you produce a lot","c":"規模經濟","s":"Big factories enjoy economies of scale, so they can buy expensive robots that small workshops cannot afford.","t":"大型工廠享有規模經濟,所以它們能購買小型工坊負擔不起的昂貴機器人。"},{"w":"workweek","p":"n.","d":"the number of hours or days people work each week","c":"工作週;每週工時","s":"Some experts believe robots could give us a shorter workweek, so people would have more time for family and hobbies.","t":"一些專家認為機器人能讓我們的每週工時變短,這樣人們就會有更多時間陪伴家人和從事嗜好。"},{"w":"hire","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job","c":"僱用","s":"The hospital plans to hire more nurses this year, although it has also bought robots to deliver medicine.","t":"醫院計畫今年僱用更多護理師,雖然它也買了送藥的機器人。"},{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a job that is available for someone to do","c":"職缺","s":"There is a vacancy for a robot technician at the airport, and the job offers good training for young people.","t":"機場有一個機器人技術員的職缺,而且這份工作為年輕人提供很好的訓練。"},{"w":"jobseeker","p":"n.","d":"a person who is looking for a job","c":"求職者","s":"Every jobseeker at the job fair was asked about computer skills, because most companies now use some kind of automation.","t":"就業博覽會上的每一位求職者都被問到電腦技能,因為大多數公司現在都使用某種自動化。"},{"w":"craftsman","p":"n.","d":"a skilled person who makes things by hand","c":"工匠;手藝人","s":"The old craftsman still makes chairs by hand, and customers pay more because no machine can copy his work exactly.","t":"這位老工匠仍然手工製作椅子,顧客願意付更多錢,因為沒有機器能完全複製他的作品。"},{"w":"understaffed","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough workers","c":"人手不足的","s":"The restaurant was understaffed during the holidays, so the owner borrowed a robot waiter from his brother's shop.","t":"這家餐廳在假期期間人手不足,所以老闆向他哥哥的店借了一台機器人服務生。"},{"w":"time-consuming","p":"adj.","d":"taking a lot of time","c":"耗時的","s":"Checking every bottle by hand was time-consuming, so the company bought a camera system that checks them in seconds.","t":"用人工檢查每個瓶子很耗時,所以公司買了一套能在幾秒內檢查完畢的攝影系統。"},{"w":"cost-saving","p":"adj.","d":"helping to spend less money","c":"節省成本的","s":"The robots were a cost-saving idea at first, but the repair bills were higher than the managers expected.","t":"機器人起初是一個節省成本的點子,但維修費用比經理們預期的還要高。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Humans & Robots: Ethics and Society 人與機器人:倫理與社會","cards":[{"w":"uncanny valley","p":"n.phr.","d":"the uneasy feeling when a robot looks almost but not quite human","c":"恐怖谷(效應)","s":"The robot's face was almost real, but its smile felt strange, so many visitors experienced the uncanny valley.","t":"這台機器人的臉幾乎跟真的一樣,但它的微笑感覺很怪,所以許多參觀者體驗到了恐怖谷效應。"},{"w":"humanlike","p":"adj.","d":"similar to a human in looks or behaviour","c":"像人類的;擬人的","s":"The robot has a humanlike voice, so many elderly users forget that they are talking to a machine.","t":"這台機器人有像人類的聲音,所以許多年長使用者會忘記他們是在和機器說話。"},{"w":"lifelike","p":"adj.","d":"looking very real or alive","c":"栩栩如生的;逼真的","s":"The museum's robot dinosaur is so lifelike that small children hide behind their parents when it roars.","t":"博物館的機器恐龍栩栩如生,小孩子在它吼叫時都躲到父母身後。"},{"w":"sentient","p":"adj.","d":"able to feel and experience things","c":"有知覺的;有感知能力的","s":"Some people believe robots could one day become sentient, but most scientists say that is still very far away.","t":"有些人相信機器人有一天可能變得有知覺,但大多數科學家說那還非常遙遠。"},{"w":"self-aware","p":"adj.","d":"knowing that you exist and understanding your own feelings","c":"有自我意識的","s":"In the movie, the robot suddenly becomes self-aware and asks why it was created, so the scientists panic.","t":"在電影中,機器人突然變得有自我意識,並問自己為什麼被創造出來,所以科學家們驚慌失措。"},{"w":"emotionless","p":"adj.","d":"showing no feelings","c":"沒有感情的;面無表情的","s":"The robot answered in an emotionless voice, but the children still laughed when it danced badly.","t":"機器人用沒有感情的聲音回答,但孩子們看到它跳得很糟時仍然笑了出來。"},{"w":"trustworthy","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted","c":"值得信賴的","s":"People will only use self-driving taxis if they feel the cars are trustworthy, so companies share their safety records.","t":"人們只有在覺得自動駕駛計程車值得信賴時才會搭乘,所以公司會公開它們的安全紀錄。"},{"w":"distrust","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that you cannot trust someone or something","c":"不信任","s":"My grandmother has a deep distrust of machines, so she still counts her change carefully at the self-checkout.","t":"我奶奶對機器有很深的不信任,所以她在自助結帳機仍然仔細地數找回的零錢。"},{"w":"technophobia","p":"n.","d":"fear or dislike of new technology","c":"科技恐懼症","s":"His technophobia disappeared after he learned to use the robot vacuum, and now he wants a robot lawnmower too.","t":"在學會使用掃地機器人後,他的科技恐懼症就消失了,現在他還想要一台割草機器人。"},{"w":"tech-savvy","p":"adj.","d":"good at understanding and using technology","c":"精通科技的","s":"My tech-savvy niece set up our smart speaker in five minutes, while my parents had been trying for two days.","t":"我那精通科技的姪女五分鐘就設定好我們的智慧音箱,而我爸媽已經試了兩天。"},{"w":"early adopter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who uses new technology as soon as it appears","c":"早期使用者;嘗鮮者","s":"My uncle is always an early adopter, so he bought a robot dog the day it went on sale.","t":"我叔叔總是嘗鮮者,所以他在機器狗開賣當天就買了一隻。"},{"w":"Luddite","p":"n.","d":"a person who is against new technology","c":"反對新科技的人","s":"My friends call me a Luddite because I prefer paper books, but I simply enjoy the feeling of turning pages.","t":"我的朋友叫我反科技的人,因為我比較喜歡紙本書,但我只是喜歡翻頁的感覺。"},{"w":"science fiction","p":"n.phr.","d":"stories about imagined future science and technology","c":"科幻小說;科幻作品","s":"Robot helpers in every home were once just science fiction, but now many families own at least one.","t":"每個家庭都有機器人幫手曾經只是科幻小說的情節,但現在許多家庭至少擁有一台。"},{"w":"utopia","p":"n.","d":"an imagined perfect society","c":"烏托邦;理想社會","s":"Some people dream of a utopia where robots do all the work, but others fear that people would feel bored and useless.","t":"有些人夢想一個由機器人做所有工作的烏托邦,但另一些人擔心人們會覺得無聊又沒有用處。"},{"w":"rogue","p":"adj.","d":"behaving differently from what is expected, often dangerously","c":"失控的;脫序的","s":"In the story, a rogue robot escapes from the lab, so the scientists must find it before it causes trouble.","t":"在故事中,一台失控的機器人從實驗室逃出,所以科學家必須在它惹麻煩之前找到它。"},{"w":"killer robot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that can choose and attack targets by itself","c":"殺手機器人","s":"Many scientists have signed a letter against the killer robot, because they believe machines should never decide who lives or dies.","t":"許多科學家簽署了一封反對殺手機器人的信,因為他們認為機器永遠不應該決定誰生誰死。"},{"w":"military","p":"adj.","d":"connected with soldiers or the armed forces","c":"軍事的","s":"Many robots were first developed for military use, but later they were used to clean up dangerous sites.","t":"許多機器人最初是為了軍事用途而開發的,但後來被用來清理危險的地點。"},{"w":"warfare","p":"n.","d":"fighting in a war","c":"戰爭;作戰","s":"Drones have changed modern warfare, and many countries are now discussing rules to control their use.","t":"無人機改變了現代戰爭,而許多國家正在討論規範其使用的規則。"},{"w":"blame","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone is responsible for something bad","c":"責怪;歸咎","s":"When a self-driving car has an accident, should we blame the owner, or is the company that made it responsible?","t":"當一輛自動駕駛汽車發生事故時,我們應該責怪車主,還是製造它的公司該負責?"},{"w":"fault","p":"n.","d":"responsibility for a mistake or problem","c":"過錯;責任","s":"The report said the crash was not the robot's fault, because a worker had switched off the safety sensor.","t":"報告說這次碰撞不是機器人的過錯,因為有一名工人關掉了安全感測器。"},{"w":"moral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with what is right and wrong","c":"道德的","s":"Teaching a robot to make moral choices is difficult, because people themselves often disagree about what is right.","t":"教機器人做出道德抉擇很困難,因為人們自己也常常對什麼是對的意見不一。"},{"w":"dignity","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being respected and valued","c":"尊嚴","s":"Robots can help old people bathe and dress, but designers must protect their dignity and give them choices.","t":"機器人能幫老人洗澡和穿衣,但設計者必須保護他們的尊嚴並給他們選擇的權利。"},{"w":"robot rights","p":"n.phr.","d":"the idea that advanced robots should have legal protections","c":"機器人權利","s":"Our class debated robot rights today, and many students said a machine without feelings cannot have rights.","t":"我們班今天辯論了機器人權利,許多學生說沒有感情的機器不能擁有權利。"},{"w":"malicious","p":"adj.","d":"intending to cause harm","c":"惡意的","s":"A malicious hacker took control of the factory robots, so the company shut down every machine for safety.","t":"一名惡意的駭客控制了工廠的機器人,所以公司為了安全關閉了每一台機器。"},{"w":"watchdog","p":"n.","d":"a group that checks that companies follow the rules","c":"監督機構","s":"The consumer watchdog tested five home robots, and it warned that two of them recorded conversations without asking.","t":"消費者監督機構測試了五台家用機器人,並警告其中兩台在未經詢問的情況下錄下對話。"},{"w":"public opinion","p":"n.phr.","d":"what most people in a society think","c":"輿論;民意","s":"public opinion about delivery drones has changed, because people now see how quickly they bring medicine to villages.","t":"關於送貨無人機的輿論已經改變,因為人們現在看到它們多快就能把藥品送到村莊。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (abolish – entrust)","cards":[{"w":"abolish","p":"v.","d":"to officially end a law, system or practice","c":"廢除","s":"The city decided to abolish the old rule that banned robots on footpaths, so delivery robots can now reach more homes.","t":"市政府決定廢除禁止機器人走在人行道上的舊規定,所以送貨機器人現在能抵達更多住家。"},{"w":"boost","p":"v.","d":"to increase or improve something","c":"提升;促進","s":"The new robots helped boost production by thirty percent, but the managers still needed workers to check quality.","t":"新機器人幫助提升了百分之三十的產量,但經理們仍然需要工人檢查品質。"},{"w":"counter","p":"v.","d":"to act against something or reply to an argument","c":"反駁;對抗","s":"The company tried to counter fears about job losses, so it promised to train every worker for a new role.","t":"公司試圖反駁關於工作流失的憂慮,所以它承諾訓練每位工人擔任新職務。"},{"w":"discontinue","p":"v.","d":"to stop making or offering something","c":"停產;停止","s":"The company will discontinue its first home robot next year, because few people bought it and repairs were too expensive.","t":"公司明年將停產它的第一款家用機器人,因為很少人購買而且維修太昂貴。"},{"w":"embed","p":"v.","d":"to fix something firmly inside something else","c":"嵌入","s":"Engineers embed tiny sensors in the robot's skin, so it can feel when someone touches it gently.","t":"工程師在機器人的皮膚裡嵌入微小的感測器,所以它能感覺到有人輕輕地觸碰它。"},{"w":"enlist","p":"v.","d":"to ask for and get someone's help or support","c":"爭取(協助);徵召","s":"The school enlist the help of local engineers, and together they built a robot that waters the school garden.","t":"學校爭取了當地工程師的協助,他們一起製作了一台幫學校花園澆水的機器人。"},{"w":"infringe","p":"v.","d":"to break a law or limit someone's rights","c":"侵犯;違反","s":"Cameras on delivery robots may infringe people's privacy, so the city requires companies to blur faces in their videos.","t":"送貨機器人上的攝影機可能會侵犯人們的隱私,所以市政府要求公司把影片中的臉孔模糊化。"},{"w":"leverage","p":"v.","d":"to use something you have to get the best result","c":"善用;利用","s":"Small farms can leverage cheap drones to check their crops, so they do not need to hire extra helpers.","t":"小型農場可以善用便宜的無人機來檢查作物,所以它們不需要僱用額外的幫手。"},{"w":"permeate","p":"v.","d":"to spread through every part of something","c":"滲透;遍及","s":"Technology has begun to permeate every part of our lives, from the kitchen to the classroom and even the football field.","t":"科技已經開始滲透我們生活的每個部分,從廚房到教室,甚至足球場。"},{"w":"pioneer","p":"v.","d":"to be the first to develop a new idea or method","c":"開創;率先開發","s":"Japanese companies pioneer the use of robots in car factories, and other countries soon copied their methods.","t":"日本公司率先開發在汽車工廠使用機器人,而其他國家很快就模仿了它們的方法。"},{"w":"saturate","p":"v.","d":"to fill something so completely that no more can be added","c":"使飽和;充斥","s":"Cheap toy robots began to saturate the market, so prices fell and many small sellers closed their shops.","t":"便宜的玩具機器人開始充斥市場,所以價格下跌,許多小賣家關掉了店。"},{"w":"display","p":"v.","d":"to show something so people can see it","c":"展示;顯示","s":"The robot can display a smiling face on its screen, and children usually smile back at it.","t":"機器人能在螢幕上顯示一張笑臉,而孩子們通常會回以微笑。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something, especially something expensive","c":"購買","s":"The hospital plans to purchase two surgical robots next year, although each machine costs more than a house.","t":"醫院計畫明年購買兩台手術機器人,雖然每台機器的價格比一間房子還貴。"},{"w":"bypass","p":"v.","d":"to go around something or avoid a rule or system","c":"繞過;略過","s":"Some workers tried to bypass the safety sensor to work faster, but this was dangerous and the manager stopped them.","t":"有些工人試圖繞過安全感測器來加快工作速度,但這很危險,所以經理阻止了他們。"},{"w":"certify","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that something meets a standard","c":"認證;證明","s":"An independent lab must certify every delivery robot as safe, and only then can it go out on public streets.","t":"一個獨立實驗室必須認證每台送貨機器人是安全的,只有這樣它才能上公共街道。"},{"w":"complicate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more difficult to understand or do","c":"使複雜化","s":"Bad weather can complicate drone deliveries, so the company sends parcels by van when it rains heavily.","t":"惡劣天氣會使無人機送貨變得複雜,所以公司在下大雨時改用貨車送包裹。"},{"w":"conceal","p":"v.","d":"to hide something carefully","c":"隱藏;隱瞞","s":"The company tried to conceal the robot's safety problems, but a worker told a reporter and the story went viral.","t":"公司試圖隱瞞機器人的安全問題,但一名員工告訴了記者,這個新聞就爆紅了。"},{"w":"defy","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to obey, or to seem impossible","c":"違抗;挑戰(常理)","s":"The tiny robot seemed to defy gravity as it climbed up the glass wall, and the audience gasped in surprise.","t":"這台小機器人爬上玻璃牆時似乎違抗了地心引力,觀眾都驚訝得倒吸一口氣。"},{"w":"detach","p":"v.","d":"to separate one part from another","c":"拆下;分離","s":"You can detach the robot's arm in seconds, so it is easy to fit a different tool for each job.","t":"你能在幾秒內拆下機器人的手臂,所以很容易為每項工作裝上不同的工具。"},{"w":"devalue","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less important or worth less","c":"貶低;使貶值","s":"Some artists fear that robot paintings will devalue human creativity, but others enjoy working with machines.","t":"有些藝術家擔心機器人畫作會貶低人類的創造力,但另一些人喜歡和機器一起創作。"},{"w":"dictate","p":"v.","d":"to control or decide how something happens","c":"支配;決定","s":"Customer demand will dictate how fast robots spread in shops, because companies only buy machines that make money.","t":"顧客需求將決定機器人在商店普及的速度,因為公司只購買能賺錢的機器。"},{"w":"discard","p":"v.","d":"to throw away something you no longer want","c":"丟棄","s":"People often discard old electronic toys, but these toys contain metals that should be recycled.","t":"人們常常丟棄舊的電子玩具,但這些玩具含有應該被回收的金屬。"},{"w":"discredit","p":"v.","d":"to make people stop trusting someone or something","c":"使不可信;敗壞名聲","s":"One serious accident could discredit the whole self-driving industry, so companies test their cars for millions of kilometres.","t":"一次嚴重的事故就可能使整個自動駕駛產業失去信任,所以公司會讓車輛測試數百萬公里。"},{"w":"dissect","p":"v.","d":"to examine something in great detail","c":"仔細剖析;解剖","s":"The engineers will dissect every second of the crash video, so they can understand exactly what went wrong.","t":"工程師將仔細剖析撞擊影片的每一秒,這樣他們就能確切了解哪裡出了問題。"},{"w":"entrust","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the job of looking after something","c":"託付;委託","s":"Would you entrust your baby to a robot nanny, or would you always prefer a human babysitter?","t":"你會把你的寶寶託付給機器人保母,還是你總是比較喜歡人類保母?"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (expire – revive)","cards":[{"w":"expire","p":"v.","d":"to come to the end of the time it is valid","c":"到期;過期","s":"The robot's software licence will expire next month, so the school must pay again or it will stop working.","t":"機器人的軟體授權下個月將到期,所以學校必須再付費,否則它會停止運作。"},{"w":"falter","p":"v.","d":"to become weaker or less certain","c":"衰退;動搖","s":"Sales of home robots began to falter last year, because many families felt they were too expensive.","t":"家用機器人的銷售去年開始衰退,因為許多家庭覺得它們太貴了。"},{"w":"forfeit","p":"v.","d":"to lose something because you broke a rule","c":"喪失;被沒收","s":"The robot team had to forfeit the match, because their machine was heavier than the competition rules allowed.","t":"這支機器人隊伍必須棄權這場比賽,因為他們的機器比比賽規則允許的還重。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"v.","d":"to make something increase or grow stronger","c":"助長;加劇","s":"News stories about killer robots fuel public fear, although most robots simply clean floors or pack boxes.","t":"有關殺手機器人的新聞助長了大眾的恐懼,雖然大多數機器人只是拖地或包裝箱子。"},{"w":"ignite","p":"v.","d":"to start a strong feeling, argument or interest","c":"引發;點燃","s":"The robot umpire's first wrong call managed to ignite a heated debate, and fans argued about it online for days.","t":"機器人裁判的第一次誤判就引發了激烈的爭論,球迷們在網路上爭論了好幾天。"},{"w":"imitate","p":"v.","d":"to copy the way someone does something","c":"模仿","s":"The robot learned to imitate the chef's movements, so it can now make noodles almost as well as he does.","t":"這台機器人學會了模仿廚師的動作,所以它現在幾乎能做出跟他一樣好的麵。"},{"w":"inflict","p":"v.","d":"to cause something bad to happen to someone","c":"造成(傷害);施加","s":"A heavy factory robot could inflict serious injuries, so workers must stay outside the yellow line at all times.","t":"一台沉重的工廠機器人可能會造成嚴重的傷害,所以工人必須隨時待在黃線外面。"},{"w":"intercept","p":"v.","d":"to stop something before it reaches its destination","c":"攔截","s":"Security staff used a special device to intercept the drone, because it was flying too close to the airport.","t":"保全人員使用一種特殊裝置來攔截無人機,因為它飛得太靠近機場了。"},{"w":"interrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop something or someone for a short time","c":"打斷;中斷","s":"A power cut can interrupt the whole production line, so the factory keeps a backup generator ready.","t":"一次停電就可能中斷整條生產線,所以工廠準備了一台備用發電機。"},{"w":"lag","p":"v.","d":"to move or develop more slowly than others","c":"落後;延遲","s":"Small companies often lag behind in using robots, because they cannot afford the high starting costs.","t":"小公司在使用機器人方面常常落後,因為它們負擔不起高昂的初期成本。"},{"w":"merge","p":"v.","d":"to combine two or more things into one","c":"合併;融合","s":"The two robot companies decided to merge, so they could share their research and compete with bigger firms.","t":"這兩家機器人公司決定合併,這樣它們就能分享研究成果並和更大的公司競爭。"},{"w":"nullify","p":"v.","d":"to make something have no effect","c":"使無效;抵銷","s":"A single loose cable can nullify months of careful work, so the team checks everything twice before each test.","t":"一條鬆脫的電纜就可能抵銷好幾個月的細心努力,所以團隊在每次測試前都會檢查兩遍。"},{"w":"obstruct","p":"v.","d":"to block a path or stop progress","c":"阻擋;妨礙","s":"Parked bicycles often obstruct the delivery robots on the pavement, so they have to wait or find another way.","t":"停放的腳踏車常常阻擋人行道上的送貨機器人,所以它們必須等待或另找路線。"},{"w":"outperform","p":"v.","d":"to do better than someone or something","c":"表現優於;勝過","s":"The new robot can outperform human workers at sorting letters, but it still struggles with handwritten addresses.","t":"新機器人在分類信件方面能勝過人類員工,但它在處理手寫地址時仍有困難。"},{"w":"outnumber","p":"v.","d":"to be greater in number than another group","c":"數量超過","s":"In some factories, robots now outnumber human workers, but people are still needed to plan and repair.","t":"在一些工廠裡,機器人的數量現在已經超過人類員工,但仍然需要人來規劃和修理。"},{"w":"outpace","p":"v.","d":"to go faster or develop more quickly than others","c":"超越;比…發展更快","s":"Technology often outpace the law, so new robots appear before governments have written rules for them.","t":"科技常常發展得比法律更快,所以新機器人在政府制定相關規則之前就出現了。"},{"w":"overshadow","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less important","c":"使相形見絀;蓋過","s":"The robot's mistake seemed to overshadow the team's great result, although they had won every other match.","t":"機器人的失誤似乎蓋過了這支隊伍的好成績,雖然他們贏了其他每一場比賽。"},{"w":"overtake","p":"v.","d":"to become greater or more successful than something","c":"超越;趕上","s":"Online shopping overtook store shopping in many cities last year, so warehouses needed many more robots.","t":"去年在許多城市,網路購物超越了實體店購物,所以倉庫需要多得多的機器人。"},{"w":"procure","p":"v.","d":"to get something, often with effort","c":"取得;採購","s":"The school worked hard to procure funding for a robot club, and now forty students meet there every Friday.","t":"學校努力取得機器人社團的經費,現在每週五有四十名學生在那裡聚會。"},{"w":"redefine","p":"v.","d":"to change the meaning or nature of something","c":"重新定義","s":"Robots will redefine what it means to have a job, because many tasks will be shared between people and machines.","t":"機器人將重新定義擁有一份工作的意義,因為許多任務將由人和機器共同分擔。"},{"w":"renew","p":"v.","d":"to start again or make something valid for longer","c":"更新;續約","s":"The factory decided to renew its contract with the robot company, because the machines had worked well for five years.","t":"工廠決定和機器人公司續約,因為這些機器已經運作良好五年了。"},{"w":"repel","p":"v.","d":"to push away or keep something away","c":"排斥;驅趕","s":"The farm uses small robots that repel birds from the fields, so farmers no longer need loud noise machines.","t":"農場使用能驅趕田裡鳥類的小型機器人,所以農夫不再需要吵鬧的噪音機器。"},{"w":"reshape","p":"v.","d":"to change the form or structure of something","c":"重塑;改變…的面貌","s":"Robots will reshape the job market over the next twenty years, so students should learn skills that machines cannot copy.","t":"機器人將在未來二十年重塑就業市場,所以學生應該學習機器無法複製的技能。"},{"w":"revamp","p":"v.","d":"to change something to improve it","c":"改造;翻新","s":"The supermarket decided to revamp its checkout area, so it added robots and removed half of the old counters.","t":"超市決定改造它的結帳區,所以它增加了機器人並撤掉一半的舊櫃台。"},{"w":"revive","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to life or use","c":"使復甦;重振","s":"Some people hope robots will revive small towns, because companies could open factories there without needing many workers.","t":"有些人希望機器人能重振小鎮,因為公司可以在那裡開設工廠而不需要很多工人。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (scrap – weaken)","cards":[{"w":"scrap","p":"v.","d":"to get rid of a plan or object that is not useful","c":"放棄;廢棄","s":"The company decided to scrap its plan for robot taxis, because the cars kept getting confused in heavy traffic.","t":"公司決定放棄機器人計程車計畫,因為那些車在交通繁忙時一直搞混方向。"},{"w":"tailor","p":"v.","d":"to make or change something for a particular person or purpose","c":"量身打造;調整","s":"The software can tailor each robot's movements to the size of the worker, so nobody has to bend uncomfortably.","t":"這套軟體能根據工人的身材調整每台機器人的動作,所以沒有人需要不舒服地彎腰。"},{"w":"unveil","p":"v.","d":"to show something new to the public for the first time","c":"發表;揭幕","s":"The company will unveil its newest robot at the technology fair, and journalists from fifty countries will attend.","t":"公司將在科技展上發表它最新的機器人,來自五十個國家的記者都會出席。"},{"w":"withdraw","p":"v.","d":"to take something back or remove it","c":"撤回;收回","s":"The company withdrew the toy robot from shops after parents reported that it got very hot when charging.","t":"在家長反映這款玩具機器人充電時會變得很燙後,公司把它從商店撤回了。"},{"w":"appraise","p":"v.","d":"to judge how good or valuable something is","c":"評估;估價","s":"Experts were invited to appraise the robot's performance, and they agreed that it was ready for use in hospitals.","t":"專家受邀評估這台機器人的表現,他們一致認為它已經可以在醫院使用了。"},{"w":"compress","p":"v.","d":"to press or make something smaller","c":"壓縮","s":"The recycling robot can compress plastic bottles into small blocks, so the trucks can carry much more each trip.","t":"這台回收機器人能把塑膠瓶壓縮成小方塊,所以卡車每趟能載運更多。"},{"w":"decentralise","p":"v.","d":"to move control from one central place to many places","c":"分散(權力或管理)","s":"Small robots could help decentralise manufacturing, so products might be made in local workshops instead of giant factories.","t":"小型機器人能幫助分散製造業,所以產品可能會在當地工坊而不是巨型工廠裡製造。"},{"w":"disable","p":"v.","d":"to stop a machine or system from working","c":"停用;使失效","s":"Workers must disable the robot before they enter its area, or it could start moving without warning.","t":"工人進入機器人的區域前必須先將它停用,否則它可能會毫無預警地開始移動。"},{"w":"enlarge","p":"v.","d":"to make something bigger","c":"擴大;放大","s":"The factory plans to enlarge its robot testing area, because the new machines are much bigger than the old ones.","t":"工廠計畫擴大機器人測試區,因為新機器比舊機器大得多。"},{"w":"execute","p":"v.","d":"to carry out a plan, order or task","c":"執行","s":"The robot can execute hundreds of tiny movements every minute, and it never loses concentration like tired workers do.","t":"這台機器人每分鐘能執行數百個細微動作,而且它從不像疲倦的工人那樣分心。"},{"w":"forbid","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone must not do something","c":"禁止","s":"The park rules forbid flying drones near the children's playground, so we took ours to an open field instead.","t":"公園的規定禁止在兒童遊樂場附近放無人機,所以我們把我們的帶到一片空地去。"},{"w":"halt","p":"v.","d":"to stop something completely","c":"停止;中止","s":"The factory had to halt production for a week, because a computer virus had attacked the robots' software.","t":"工廠必須停止生產一星期,因為電腦病毒攻擊了機器人的軟體。"},{"w":"hover","p":"v.","d":"to stay in the air in one place","c":"盤旋;懸停","s":"The drone can hover above the building for twenty minutes, and it sends pictures of the roof to the repair team.","t":"這架無人機能在大樓上方懸停二十分鐘,並把屋頂的照片傳給維修團隊。"},{"w":"manoeuvre","p":"v.","d":"to move something carefully through a difficult space","c":"(靈活)操控;移動","s":"The delivery robot must manoeuvre around people and dogs on busy pavements, so it moves slowly in crowded areas.","t":"送貨機器人必須在繁忙的人行道上繞過行人和狗靈活移動,所以它在擁擠區域行進得很慢。"},{"w":"mount","p":"v.","d":"to fix something onto a wall, stand or vehicle","c":"安裝;架設","s":"The workers will mount a camera on top of the robot, so it can see over the boxes in front of it.","t":"工人將在機器人頂部安裝一台攝影機,這樣它就能看到前方箱子的另一邊。"},{"w":"prescribe","p":"v.","d":"to say officially what must be done","c":"規定;開(藥)","s":"Safety laws prescribe how far workers must stand from moving robots, and inspectors check this every year.","t":"安全法規規定工人必須和移動中的機器人保持多遠的距離,而檢查員每年都會查核。"},{"w":"regain","p":"v.","d":"to get something back after losing it","c":"恢復;重新獲得","s":"After the stroke, my grandmother used a robot glove to regain the use of her hand, and now she can write again.","t":"中風後,我奶奶使用機器人手套來恢復手部功能,現在她又能寫字了。"},{"w":"reinvent","p":"v.","d":"to change something so much that it seems completely new","c":"徹底改造;重新發明","s":"The camera company had to reinvent itself when phones replaced cameras, so it started making parts for robots.","t":"當手機取代相機時,這家相機公司必須徹底改造自己,於是它開始製造機器人零件。"},{"w":"resume","p":"v.","d":"to start again after a pause","c":"恢復;重新開始","s":"The match will resume after the referee checks the video, so the players are waiting in the middle of the field.","t":"比賽將在裁判檢查影片後恢復進行,所以球員們正在球場中央等待。"},{"w":"rotate","p":"v.","d":"to turn around a central point","c":"旋轉;輪流","s":"The robot's wrist can rotate in a full circle, so it can screw lids onto jars faster than any worker.","t":"機器人的手腕能旋轉一整圈,所以它把蓋子轉緊在罐子上的速度比任何工人都快。"},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"v.","d":"to give up something valuable for something more important","c":"犧牲","s":"Some companies sacrifice quality for speed, but customers soon notice the problems and stop buying their products.","t":"有些公司為了速度而犧牲品質,但顧客很快就會注意到問題並停止購買他們的產品。"},{"w":"shield","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from harm","c":"保護;遮擋","s":"The robot's metal cover shield its electronic parts from dust, so it can work in dirty factories for years.","t":"機器人的金屬外殼保護它的電子零件不受灰塵影響,所以它能在骯髒的工廠裡工作好幾年。"},{"w":"strengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"強化;加強","s":"The government wants to strengthen safety rules for drones, because several have crashed into homes this year.","t":"政府想要加強無人機的安全規範,因為今年已有好幾架撞進民宅。"},{"w":"uncover","p":"v.","d":"to discover something that was hidden","c":"揭露;發現","s":"Reporters managed to uncover the truth about the robot accident, and the company was forced to apologise.","t":"記者成功揭露了機器人事故的真相,公司被迫道歉。"},{"w":"weaken","p":"v.","d":"to make something less strong","c":"削弱","s":"Cheap robots from abroad could weaken local factories, so the government is offering them money to modernise.","t":"來自國外的便宜機器人可能會削弱本地工廠,所以政府提供資金幫助它們現代化。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (outlast – deadlock)","cards":[{"w":"outlast","p":"v.","d":"to continue working or living longer than something else","c":"比…更持久","s":"These robot batteries outlast the old ones by several hours, so the machines can work through a whole night shift.","t":"這些機器人電池比舊電池更持久好幾個小時,所以機器能撐過整個夜班。"},{"w":"advancement","p":"n.","d":"progress or development in something","c":"進步;發展","s":"Recent advancement in battery technology have made robots lighter, and they can now work longer without charging.","t":"近來電池技術的進步讓機器人變得更輕,而且它們現在不必充電就能工作更久。"},{"w":"array","p":"n.","d":"a large group or range of things","c":"一系列;大量","s":"The robot carries an array of sensors on its head, so it can measure heat, light and sound at the same time.","t":"這台機器人頭上搭載了一系列感測器,所以它能同時測量熱度、光線和聲音。"},{"w":"asset","p":"n.","d":"something or someone that is useful and valuable","c":"資產;寶貴的人或物","s":"The robot became a real asset to the small bakery, because it could knead dough while the baker served customers.","t":"這台機器人成為小麵包店真正的資產,因為它能在麵包師傅招呼顧客時揉麵團。"},{"w":"bottleneck","p":"n.","d":"a point where things slow down and cause delays","c":"瓶頸","s":"Packing was the main bottleneck in the warehouse, so the manager bought two robots to speed it up.","t":"包裝是倉庫裡主要的瓶頸,所以經理買了兩台機器人來加快速度。"},{"w":"demise","p":"n.","d":"the end or failure of something","c":"消亡;倒閉","s":"Many people predicted the demise of the bank teller, but most banks still keep some staff to help customers.","t":"許多人預測銀行櫃員會消失,但大多數銀行仍然保留一些員工來協助顧客。"},{"w":"diffusion","p":"n.","d":"the spreading of something over a wide area or among many people","c":"擴散;普及","s":"The diffusion of robots into small businesses has been slow, because the machines are still quite expensive.","t":"機器人在小型企業中的普及一直很緩慢,因為這些機器仍然相當昂貴。"},{"w":"provision","p":"n.","d":"the act of supplying something people need","c":"提供;供應","s":"The provision of free robot training for workers is important, because it helps them find new jobs quickly.","t":"為工人提供免費的機器人訓練很重要,因為這能幫助他們很快找到新工作。"},{"w":"channel","p":"n.","d":"a way of sending information or goods","c":"管道;頻道","s":"The company uses social media as its main channel for robot news, so fans can watch new videos every week.","t":"公司把社群媒體當作機器人新聞的主要管道,所以粉絲每週都能看到新影片。"},{"w":"clause","p":"n.","d":"a part of a contract or legal document","c":"條款","s":"The contract includes a clause about robot accidents, so both companies know who must pay if something goes wrong.","t":"合約中包含一條關於機器人事故的條款,所以兩家公司都知道出事時由誰負責賠償。"},{"w":"contract","p":"n.","d":"a written legal agreement between people or companies","c":"合約","s":"The robot company signed a contract with the airport, and its robots will clean the floors for the next three years.","t":"這家機器人公司和機場簽了一份合約,它的機器人將在未來三年清潔地板。"},{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"the money used in a country","c":"貨幣","s":"The robot at the airport can exchange currency for travellers, and it shows the rate clearly on its screen.","t":"機場的機器人能為旅客兌換貨幣,並在螢幕上清楚地顯示匯率。"},{"w":"design","p":"n.","d":"the way something is planned and made","c":"設計","s":"The robot's simple design makes it easy to repair, so even school students can replace its broken parts.","t":"這台機器人簡單的設計讓它很容易修理,所以連學生都能更換它壞掉的零件。"},{"w":"environment","p":"n.","d":"the conditions and surroundings where something works","c":"環境","s":"Robots work well in a controlled environment like a factory, but they still struggle on rocky ground or in heavy rain.","t":"機器人在像工廠這樣受控的環境中運作良好,但它們在崎嶇地面或大雨中仍有困難。"},{"w":"finance","p":"n.","d":"money, or the management of money","c":"資金;財務","s":"The start-up needed more finance to build its farming robots, so it asked several investors for help.","t":"這家新創公司需要更多資金來製造農業機器人,所以它向幾位投資人尋求協助。"},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"a stage in the development of a product","c":"世代;代","s":"The latest generation of robot vacuums can climb small steps, so they can clean several rooms without help.","t":"最新一代的掃地機器人能爬上小台階,所以它們不需協助就能打掃好幾個房間。"},{"w":"vehicle","p":"n.","d":"a machine that carries people or goods, like a car","c":"車輛;交通工具","s":"The robot vehicle carries food around the university campus, and students order it from an app on their phones.","t":"這輛機器人車輛在大學校園裡運送食物,學生用手機上的應用程式點餐。"},{"w":"acclaim","p":"n.","d":"public praise for something","c":"讚譽;喝采","s":"The young inventors won international acclaim for their cheap robot hand, and hospitals in many countries now use it.","t":"這些年輕發明家以他們便宜的機器手贏得了國際讚譽,現在許多國家的醫院都在使用它。"},{"w":"adversary","p":"n.","d":"an enemy or opponent","c":"對手;敵手","s":"The chess robot was a tough adversary, but the young player studied its moves and finally beat it.","t":"這台下棋機器人是一個難纏的對手,但這位年輕棋手研究了它的棋路,最後打敗了它。"},{"w":"arena","p":"n.","d":"a large place for sports or shows; an area of activity","c":"競技場;舞台(領域)","s":"The robot fighting competition was held in a huge arena, and thousands of fans shouted for their favourite machines.","t":"機器人格鬥比賽在一座巨大的競技場舉行,數千名粉絲為他們最喜愛的機器吶喊。"},{"w":"backlash","p":"n.","d":"a strong negative reaction from many people","c":"強烈反彈","s":"There was a public backlash when the supermarket replaced all its cashiers, so it brought some of them back.","t":"當超市取代所有收銀員時引發了大眾的強烈反彈,所以它讓其中一些人回來工作。"},{"w":"cluster","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things close together","c":"群聚;聚落","s":"A cluster of robot companies has grown up around the university, because they want to hire its graduates.","t":"一群機器人公司在大學周圍發展起來,因為它們想僱用該校的畢業生。"},{"w":"consortium","p":"n.","d":"a group of companies working together on a project","c":"聯盟;財團","s":"A consortium of car makers is developing a shared system for self-driving cars, so they can all save money.","t":"一個汽車製造商聯盟正在開發共用的自動駕駛系統,這樣它們全都能省錢。"},{"w":"conundrum","p":"n.","d":"a confusing and difficult problem","c":"難題;謎題","s":"Self-driving cars face a moral conundrum: should they protect the passenger or the person crossing the road?","t":"自動駕駛汽車面臨一個道德難題:它們應該保護乘客還是過馬路的人?"},{"w":"deadlock","p":"n.","d":"a situation where no progress can be made because people disagree","c":"僵局","s":"The talks about robot rules reached a deadlock, because neither the companies nor the workers would change their position.","t":"關於機器人規範的談判陷入了僵局,因為公司和工人雙方都不願改變立場。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (forum – vicinity)","cards":[{"w":"forum","p":"n.","d":"a meeting or website where people discuss ideas","c":"論壇","s":"The city held a public forum about delivery robots, and many residents shared their worries about safety.","t":"市政府舉辦了一場關於送貨機器人的公開論壇,許多居民分享了他們對安全的擔憂。"},{"w":"friction","p":"n.","d":"disagreement between people; or rubbing between surfaces","c":"摩擦;衝突","s":"The new robots caused some friction between managers and workers, so the company held meetings to listen to everyone.","t":"新機器人在經理和工人之間造成了一些摩擦,所以公司舉行會議聆聽每個人的意見。"},{"w":"hallmark","p":"n.","d":"a typical feature that shows what something is like","c":"特點;標誌","s":"Smooth, quiet movement is the hallmark of a well-designed robot, and engineers spend years trying to achieve it.","t":"流暢安靜的動作是設計精良的機器人的特點,而工程師花了好幾年試圖做到這一點。"},{"w":"hurdle","p":"n.","d":"a problem you must solve before you can make progress","c":"障礙;難關","s":"Cost is still the biggest hurdle for home robots, but prices are falling a little every year.","t":"價格仍然是家用機器人最大的障礙,但價格每年都在稍微下降。"},{"w":"inception","p":"n.","d":"the start of an organisation or activity","c":"開端;創立","s":"Since its inception in 2015, the robot club has grown from five members to more than a hundred.","t":"自從2015年創立以來,這個機器人社團已經從五名成員成長到一百多人。"},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"one of the things needed to make something successful","c":"要素;成分","s":"Teamwork was the key ingredient in our robot project, because nobody could build every part alone.","t":"團隊合作是我們機器人專題中的關鍵要素,因為沒有人能獨自製作每個零件。"},{"w":"jurisdiction","p":"n.","d":"the official power to make legal decisions in an area","c":"管轄權;管轄範圍","s":"Drone rules differ in each jurisdiction, so pilots must check the local laws before they fly in a new city.","t":"每個管轄區的無人機規定都不同,所以操作者在新城市飛行前必須查看當地法規。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"an important event or step in development","c":"里程碑;地標","s":"The first robot surgery was a landmark in medical history, and it encouraged hospitals around the world to try the technology.","t":"第一次機器人手術是醫學史上的一個里程碑,它鼓勵了世界各地的醫院嘗試這項技術。"},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"something left behind from the past that still has effects","c":"遺產;遺留影響","s":"The old factory's legacy is still visible in the town, but now the building is used as a robot museum.","t":"老工廠的遺留影響在鎮上仍然可見,但現在這棟建築被用作機器人博物館。"},{"w":"monopoly","p":"n.","d":"complete control of a market by one company","c":"壟斷;獨占","s":"One company had a monopoly on surgical robots for years, so hospitals had to pay whatever price it asked.","t":"一家公司多年來壟斷了手術機器人市場,所以醫院必須支付它開出的任何價格。"},{"w":"outlay","p":"n.","d":"the money spent on something, especially at the start","c":"(初期)支出;花費","s":"The initial outlay for the robots was high, but the farm saved money on labour within three years.","t":"購買機器人的初期支出很高,但農場在三年內就在人力成本上省回了錢。"},{"w":"parity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being equal","c":"平等;同等","s":"Robots have nearly reached parity with humans at sorting fruit, but they are still slower at picking delicate berries.","t":"機器人在水果分類方面幾乎已經和人類達到同等水準,但在採摘嬌嫩的莓果時仍然比較慢。"},{"w":"patent","p":"n.","d":"an official right to be the only one to make an invention","c":"專利","s":"The student applied for a patent on her robot design, because she did not want big companies to copy it.","t":"這位學生為她的機器人設計申請了專利,因為她不想讓大公司抄襲。"},{"w":"pitfall","p":"n.","d":"a hidden problem or danger","c":"陷阱;隱患","s":"One pitfall of home robots is that they collect a lot of data, so users should check the privacy settings carefully.","t":"家用機器人的一個隱患是它們會收集大量資料,所以使用者應該仔細檢查隱私設定。"},{"w":"precaution","p":"n.","d":"something done to prevent harm in the future","c":"預防措施","s":"As a safety precaution, all workers wear bright vests, so the robots can see them clearly in the warehouse.","t":"作為安全預防措施,所有工人都穿著鮮豔的背心,這樣機器人在倉庫裡就能清楚地看到他們。"},{"w":"realm","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity or interest","c":"領域;範疇","s":"Robots that cook full meals are no longer in the realm of fantasy, because several restaurants already use them.","t":"能烹煮整頓飯的機器人不再屬於幻想的範疇,因為已經有幾家餐廳在使用它們。"},{"w":"stakeholder","p":"n.","d":"a person or group affected by a decision","c":"利害關係人","s":"Every stakeholder, including workers, customers and neighbours, was invited to give opinions before the robot factory was built.","t":"每一位利害關係人,包括工人、顧客和鄰居,都在機器人工廠興建前受邀提供意見。"},{"w":"standpoint","p":"n.","d":"a way of looking at or judging a situation","c":"立場;觀點","s":"From a safety standpoint, robots are a great help, but from a social one, they raise difficult questions.","t":"從安全的觀點來看,機器人是很大的幫助,但從社會的觀點來看,它們引發了困難的問題。"},{"w":"synergy","p":"n.","d":"the extra power produced when people or things work together","c":"綜效;協同作用","s":"There is real synergy between the nurses and the robots, because each does what it is best at.","t":"護理師和機器人之間有真正的協同作用,因為各自做自己最擅長的事。"},{"w":"upheaval","p":"n.","d":"a big change that causes confusion or difficulty","c":"劇變;動盪","s":"The arrival of robots caused great upheaval in the town, so many families moved away to find new jobs.","t":"機器人的到來在小鎮引起了巨大的動盪,所以許多家庭搬走去找新工作。"},{"w":"utility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being useful","c":"效用;實用性","s":"The utility of a robot depends on the job it does, so a cheap cleaning robot may be more valuable than a fancy one.","t":"一台機器人的實用性取決於它所做的工作,所以一台便宜的清潔機器人可能比一台花俏的更有價值。"},{"w":"venture","p":"n.","d":"a new business activity that involves risk","c":"(冒險)事業;新創企業","s":"Their robot delivery venture failed in the first year, but they learned a lot and started a better company later.","t":"他們的機器人送貨事業在第一年就失敗了,但他們學到很多,後來創立了一家更好的公司。"},{"w":"verdict","p":"n.","d":"an opinion or decision after testing or judging something","c":"評價;裁決","s":"The teachers' verdict on the classroom robot was positive, although they said it needed a quieter voice.","t":"老師們對教室機器人的評價是正面的,雖然他們說它需要更小聲一點的聲音。"},{"w":"viewpoint","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of thinking about something","c":"觀點;看法","s":"From the customer's viewpoint, robot waiters are fun, but many restaurant workers see them as a threat to their jobs.","t":"從顧客的觀點來看,機器人服務生很有趣,但許多餐廳員工把它們視為對工作的威脅。"},{"w":"vicinity","p":"n.","d":"the area near a particular place","c":"附近;鄰近地區","s":"Drones are not allowed in the vicinity of the airport, so the police stopped a man who was flying one there.","t":"機場附近不允許無人機飛行,所以警察攔下了一名在那裡放無人機的男子。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (agenda – adjustable)","cards":[{"w":"agenda","p":"n.","d":"a list of things to discuss or plans to carry out","c":"議程;待辦事項","s":"Robot safety was at the top of the meeting's agenda, because a worker had been hurt the week before.","t":"機器人安全排在會議議程的首位,因為前一週有一名工人受傷了。"},{"w":"aftermath","p":"n.","d":"the period after a bad event","c":"(災難等的)後果;餘波","s":"In the aftermath of the earthquake, rescue robots searched the broken buildings, so firefighters could stay out of danger.","t":"在地震的餘波中,救援機器人搜尋倒塌的建築物,所以消防員可以遠離危險。"},{"w":"breakdown","p":"n.","d":"a failure of a machine to work","c":"故障;崩潰","s":"A breakdown in the main robot stopped the whole line, so the company now keeps a spare machine ready.","t":"主要機器人的故障讓整條生產線停擺,所以公司現在會準備一台備用機器。"},{"w":"coverage","p":"n.","d":"the reporting of news about something","c":"新聞報導;報導範圍","s":"The robot football match got a lot of media coverage, and our school's team appeared on the evening news.","t":"這場機器人足球賽得到很多媒體報導,而我們學校的隊伍出現在晚間新聞上。"},{"w":"feat","p":"n.","d":"an impressive achievement that needs skill or strength","c":"壯舉;非凡成就","s":"Running a full marathon was an amazing feat for a robot, although it needed three battery changes along the way.","t":"跑完一場全程馬拉松對機器人來說是驚人的壯舉,雖然它途中需要換三次電池。"},{"w":"footage","p":"n.","d":"film or video of an event","c":"影片片段;錄影畫面","s":"Video footage showed that the robot had stopped in time, so the company was not blamed for the accident.","t":"錄影畫面顯示機器人及時停下,所以公司沒有因這次事故而被責怪。"},{"w":"overview","p":"n.","d":"a short description of the main points","c":"概述;概要","s":"The teacher gave us a quick overview of robot history, and then we watched a video of the first factory robots.","t":"老師給我們一個簡短的機器人歷史概述,然後我們觀看了第一批工廠機器人的影片。"},{"w":"pinnacle","p":"n.","d":"the highest point of achievement","c":"巔峰;頂點","s":"Winning the world robot championship was the pinnacle of her career, but she still enjoys teaching beginners.","t":"贏得世界機器人錦標賽是她職涯的巔峰,但她仍然喜歡教初學者。"},{"w":"portfolio","p":"n.","d":"a range of products, or a collection of someone's work","c":"產品組合;作品集","s":"The company's portfolio includes robots for farms, hospitals and homes, so it does not depend on a single market.","t":"這家公司的產品組合包括農場、醫院和家庭用的機器人,所以它不依賴單一市場。"},{"w":"proposition","p":"n.","d":"an idea, offer or plan to consider","c":"提議;主張","s":"A robot that costs less than a phone is an attractive proposition, but customers want to know how long it will last.","t":"一台比手機還便宜的機器人是很有吸引力的提議,但顧客想知道它能用多久。"},{"w":"rival","p":"n.","d":"a person or company competing with another","c":"競爭者;對手","s":"Our school's main rival won the robot contest last year, so we practised every weekend to beat them this time.","t":"我們學校的主要競爭對手去年贏得了機器人比賽,所以我們每個週末都練習,這次要打敗他們。"},{"w":"showcase","p":"n.","d":"an event that shows the best qualities of something","c":"展示會;展示的機會","s":"The technology fair is a showcase for young inventors, and many of them get job offers after the event.","t":"這個科技展是年輕發明家的展示舞台,許多人在活動後得到工作機會。"},{"w":"transaction","p":"n.","d":"an act of buying or selling something","c":"交易","s":"Each transaction at the robot shop is recorded on the computer, so the owner knows exactly what sold each day.","t":"機器人商店的每一筆交易都記錄在電腦上,所以老闆確切知道每天賣出了什麼。"},{"w":"turnover","p":"n.","d":"the rate at which workers leave and are replaced","c":"人員流動率;營業額","s":"The warehouse had high staff turnover because the work was boring, so the managers brought in robots for the dullest jobs.","t":"這間倉庫因為工作枯燥而人員流動率很高,所以經理們引進機器人來做最乏味的工作。"},{"w":"upkeep","p":"n.","d":"the cost or work of keeping something in good condition","c":"維護(費用);保養","s":"The upkeep of the robots costs the hotel a lot each year, so it is not sure the machines really save money.","t":"機器人的維護費用每年讓飯店花不少錢,所以飯店不確定這些機器是否真的省錢。"},{"w":"yardstick","p":"n.","d":"a standard used to judge or compare things","c":"衡量標準;準繩","s":"Speed is not the only yardstick for a good robot, because safety and reliability are just as important.","t":"速度不是衡量好機器人的唯一標準,因為安全性和可靠度同樣重要。"},{"w":"foothold","p":"n.","d":"a secure position from which to make progress","c":"立足點;據點","s":"The young company gained a foothold in the Asian market, and now it sells cleaning robots in ten countries.","t":"這家年輕的公司在亞洲市場取得了立足點,現在它在十個國家銷售清潔機器人。"},{"w":"applicable","p":"adj.","d":"affecting or relevant to a person or situation","c":"適用的","s":"The new safety rules are applicable to all robots in public places, so delivery robots must now carry warning lights.","t":"新的安全規定適用於公共場所的所有機器人,所以送貨機器人現在必須配備警示燈。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with buying, selling and making money","c":"商業的","s":"The robot was first built for research, but now the company sells it for commercial use in shops and hotels.","t":"這台機器人最初是為了研究而製造的,但現在公司把它賣給商店和飯店作商業用途。"},{"w":"customary","p":"adj.","d":"usual or traditional in a situation","c":"慣例的;習慣的","s":"It is customary to thank the shopkeeper in our town, so some people even say thank you to the robot at the till.","t":"在我們鎮上感謝店主是慣例,所以有些人甚至會對收銀台的機器人說謝謝。"},{"w":"modular","p":"adj.","d":"made of separate parts that can be joined or replaced","c":"模組化的","s":"The robot has a modular design, so if one part breaks, you can change that piece instead of buying a new robot.","t":"這台機器人採用模組化設計,所以如果一個零件壞了,你可以更換那一塊而不用買新機器人。"},{"w":"economic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with trade, industry and money","c":"經濟的","s":"Robots bring clear economic benefits to factories, but governments must also think about the workers who lose their jobs.","t":"機器人為工廠帶來明顯的經濟效益,但政府也必須考慮失去工作的工人。"},{"w":"physical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the body or real objects","c":"身體的;實體的","s":"Robots can take over the most tiring physical work, so older employees can stay in their jobs for longer.","t":"機器人能接手最累人的體力工作,所以年長員工能在職位上待得更久。"},{"w":"technical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with practical skills or machines","c":"技術的","s":"The robot stopped because of a technical problem, but the engineer fixed it quickly and the show continued.","t":"機器人因為一個技術問題而停下,但工程師很快就修好了,表演繼續進行。"},{"w":"adjustable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed to suit different needs","c":"可調整的","s":"The robot desk has an adjustable height, so both short and tall students can use it comfortably.","t":"這張機器人桌子的高度是可調整的,所以矮個子和高個子的學生都能舒服地使用。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (alarming – unmanned)","cards":[{"w":"alarming","p":"adj.","d":"causing worry or fear","c":"令人擔憂的","s":"The report showed an alarming number of drone accidents near schools, so the city introduced stricter rules.","t":"報告顯示學校附近的無人機事故數量令人擔憂,所以市政府實施了更嚴格的規定。"},{"w":"bulky","p":"adj.","d":"large and difficult to carry or move","c":"笨重的;龐大的","s":"Early robots were bulky and slow, but modern ones are small enough to fit under a kitchen table.","t":"早期的機器人既笨重又緩慢,但現代的機器人小到可以放在廚房桌子底下。"},{"w":"compact","p":"adj.","d":"small and using little space","c":"小巧的;緊湊的","s":"The new robot is very compact, so it can clean under beds and between chair legs easily.","t":"新的機器人非常小巧,所以它能輕鬆地打掃床底和椅腳之間。"},{"w":"costly","p":"adj.","d":"expensive; causing loss or damage","c":"昂貴的;代價高的","s":"Mistakes on the production line can be costly, so the company uses cameras to catch problems early.","t":"生產線上的錯誤可能代價很高,所以公司使用攝影機及早發現問題。"},{"w":"exorbitant","p":"adj.","d":"much too expensive","c":"過高的;(價格)離譜的","s":"The price of the first robot dog was exorbitant, but now similar models cost less than a new phone.","t":"第一隻機器狗的價格高得離譜,但現在類似的型號比一支新手機還便宜。"},{"w":"experimental","p":"adj.","d":"new and still being tested","c":"實驗性的","s":"The airport is using an experimental robot to guide travellers, so staff are watching closely to see how passengers react.","t":"機場正在使用一台實驗性的機器人引導旅客,所以員工密切觀察乘客的反應。"},{"w":"extraordinary","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or surprising","c":"非凡的;驚人的","s":"The robot showed extraordinary balance on the icy path, and the engineers were surprised that it never slipped.","t":"這台機器人在結冰的路上展現了驚人的平衡力,工程師們很驚訝它從未滑倒。"},{"w":"groundbreaking","p":"adj.","d":"new and very important; never done before","c":"開創性的;突破性的","s":"The team's groundbreaking research helped robots feel heat and pain, and other universities soon started similar projects.","t":"這個團隊的開創性研究幫助機器人感受熱與痛,其他大學很快也開始了類似的計畫。"},{"w":"high-tech","p":"adj.","d":"using the most modern technology","c":"高科技的","s":"The new library is very high-tech, because robots bring books to readers and return them to the shelves.","t":"新的圖書館非常高科技,因為機器人會把書送給讀者並把它們放回書架。"},{"w":"lengthy","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time","c":"冗長的;漫長的","s":"After a lengthy test period, the robot taxi was finally allowed to carry passengers in the city centre.","t":"經過漫長的測試期,機器人計程車終於獲准在市中心載客。"},{"w":"manageable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to deal with or control","c":"可控制的;應付得來的","s":"With robots doing the heavy lifting, the nurses' workload became more manageable, and they felt less tired at night.","t":"有了機器人負責搬運重物,護理師的工作量變得比較應付得來,她們晚上也覺得沒那麼累了。"},{"w":"massive","p":"adj.","d":"very large and heavy","c":"巨大的;大規模的","s":"The company made a massive investment in robots, so it expects to produce twice as many cars next year.","t":"公司在機器人上進行了大規模的投資,所以它預計明年的汽車產量將翻倍。"},{"w":"minute","p":"adj.","d":"extremely small","c":"微小的","s":"The robot can find minute cracks in aeroplane engines, so it helps keep passengers safe on every flight.","t":"這台機器人能找出飛機引擎中微小的裂縫,所以它幫助保障每趟航班的乘客安全。"},{"w":"monumental","p":"adj.","d":"very large or important","c":"巨大的;極其重要的","s":"Building a robot that truly understands people is a monumental task, and it may take scientists many more decades.","t":"打造一台真正理解人類的機器人是一項極其艱鉅的任務,科學家可能還需要好幾十年。"},{"w":"multipurpose","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used for many different jobs","c":"多用途的","s":"The farm bought a multipurpose robot that can plant seeds, pull weeds and check the soil, so it saves a lot of time.","t":"農場買了一台能播種、拔草和檢查土壤的多用途機器人,所以它節省了許多時間。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"light and easy to carry","c":"可攜帶的;輕便的","s":"The doctor carries a portable scanner to the villages, so patients do not need to travel to the city hospital.","t":"醫生帶著一台可攜式掃描儀到村莊,所以病人不需要遠赴城市的醫院。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"useful and suitable for real situations","c":"實用的","s":"A robot that folds clothes sounds fun, but a robot that washes dishes is more practical for busy families.","t":"一台會摺衣服的機器人聽起來很有趣,但對忙碌的家庭來說,一台會洗碗的機器人更實用。"},{"w":"questionable","p":"adj.","d":"not certain, or possibly wrong","c":"可疑的;值得懷疑的","s":"The robot umpire made a questionable call in the final inning, so the coach asked to see the replay.","t":"機器人裁判在最後一局做出了一個值得懷疑的判決,所以教練要求查看重播。"},{"w":"seamless","p":"adj.","d":"smooth and without problems or breaks","c":"無縫的;流暢的","s":"The robot and the nurse worked together in a seamless way, so the patient hardly noticed the machine.","t":"機器人和護理師以流暢無縫的方式合作,所以病人幾乎沒注意到那台機器。"},{"w":"sizeable","p":"adj.","d":"fairly large","c":"相當大的","s":"A sizeable number of shoppers prefer human cashiers, so the supermarket still keeps several staffed counters open.","t":"相當大比例的顧客比較喜歡人工收銀員,所以超市仍然保留好幾個有人的櫃台。"},{"w":"specialised","p":"adj.","d":"designed for one particular purpose","c":"專門的;專業化的","s":"The hospital uses specialised robots to carry blood samples, so doctors get test results much faster.","t":"醫院使用專門的機器人運送血液樣本,所以醫生能更快拿到檢驗結果。"},{"w":"superior","p":"adj.","d":"better than others in quality","c":"較優的;優越的","s":"The new camera gives the robot superior eyesight, so it can read small labels from across the room.","t":"新攝影機讓機器人擁有更優越的視力,所以它能從房間另一頭讀出小標籤。"},{"w":"inferior","p":"adj.","d":"lower in quality than others","c":"較差的;次等的","s":"Some customers think robot-made food is inferior, but blind taste tests show most people cannot tell the difference.","t":"有些顧客認為機器人做的食物比較差,但盲測顯示大多數人吃不出差別。"},{"w":"unattended","p":"adj.","d":"not watched or looked after by anyone","c":"無人看管的","s":"Never leave a charging robot unattended for hours, because faulty batteries can sometimes overheat and start fires.","t":"絕對不要讓充電中的機器人無人看管好幾個小時,因為有問題的電池有時會過熱並引發火災。"},{"w":"unmanned","p":"adj.","d":"operating without a person on board","c":"無人駕駛的;無人操作的","s":"An unmanned boat collected rubbish from the lake, so volunteers no longer had to paddle out in the cold.","t":"一艘無人駕駛的船收集了湖上的垃圾,所以志工們不再需要在寒冷中划船出去。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (unrivalled – swiftly)","cards":[{"w":"unrivalled","p":"adj.","d":"better than any other","c":"無與倫比的","s":"The factory's robots have unrivalled speed, so they can produce ten thousand phones every single day.","t":"這間工廠的機器人有無與倫比的速度,所以它們每天能生產一萬支手機。"},{"w":"wholesale","p":"adj.","d":"happening on a very large scale, affecting many things","c":"全面的;大規模的","s":"Experts warn that wholesale automation could leave many people without work, so they want governments to prepare now.","t":"專家警告大規模的自動化可能讓許多人失業,所以他們希望政府現在就做好準備。"},{"w":"crude","p":"adj.","d":"simple and not carefully made","c":"粗糙的;簡陋的","s":"Our first robot was quite crude, but it could move forward and turn, and we were very proud of it.","t":"我們的第一台機器人相當粗糙,但它能前進和轉彎,我們為它感到非常自豪。"},{"w":"delicate","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged; needing care","c":"脆弱的;精細的","s":"Picking strawberries is a delicate job, so the robot uses soft fingers that will not crush the fruit.","t":"採草莓是一項精細的工作,所以機器人使用不會把果實壓爛的柔軟手指。"},{"w":"dire","p":"adj.","d":"very serious or terrible","c":"極嚴重的;可怕的","s":"Some writers make dire predictions about robots taking every job, but history shows new jobs usually appear.","t":"一些作家對機器人奪走所有工作做出可怕的預測,但歷史顯示通常會出現新的工作。"},{"w":"eligible","p":"adj.","d":"allowed to do or receive something","c":"有資格的;符合條件的","s":"Workers who lost jobs to robots are eligible for free training, so many of them are learning computer skills.","t":"因機器人而失去工作的工人有資格接受免費訓練,所以他們之中許多人正在學習電腦技能。"},{"w":"fierce","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or intense","c":"激烈的;猛烈的","s":"Competition between robot companies is fierce, so prices have dropped and quality has improved quickly.","t":"機器人公司之間的競爭很激烈,所以價格下降了,品質也很快地提升了。"},{"w":"mobile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move easily from place to place","c":"可移動的","s":"The hospital has a mobile robot that travels between floors, and it can even take the lift by itself.","t":"醫院有一台在樓層間移動的可移動式機器人,它甚至能自己搭電梯。"},{"w":"sleek","p":"adj.","d":"smooth, shiny and attractive in shape","c":"線條流暢的;時髦的","s":"The new robot has a sleek white body, so it looks more like a piece of furniture than a machine.","t":"新機器人有線條流暢的白色機身,所以它看起來更像一件家具而不是一台機器。"},{"w":"steep","p":"adj.","d":"very large or sudden; or rising sharply","c":"陡峭的;急劇的","s":"There has been a steep rise in robot sales since last year, because prices have dropped and quality has improved.","t":"自去年以來機器人的銷售量急劇上升,因為價格下降而品質提升了。"},{"w":"sturdy","p":"adj.","d":"strong and not easily broken","c":"堅固的;結實的","s":"The farm robot needs sturdy wheels, because it has to drive over rocks and through mud every day.","t":"農場機器人需要堅固的輪子,因為它每天都必須開過石頭和穿過泥巴。"},{"w":"tireless","p":"adj.","d":"working hard without getting tired","c":"不知疲倦的","s":"Robots are tireless workers, but they cannot comfort a crying child or understand a joke.","t":"機器人是不知疲倦的工作者,但它們無法安慰哭泣的孩子或聽懂笑話。"},{"w":"exclusively","p":"adv.","d":"only; not including anything else","c":"專門地;僅僅","s":"The robot is used exclusively for cleaning the hospital floors, so it never enters the patients' rooms.","t":"這台機器人專門用來清潔醫院的地板,所以它從不進入病房。"},{"w":"indefinitely","p":"adv.","d":"for a period with no fixed end","c":"無限期地","s":"The robot taxi service was stopped indefinitely after the accident, and nobody knows when it will start again.","t":"事故發生後,機器人計程車服務被無限期暫停,沒有人知道它何時會再開始。"},{"w":"increasingly","p":"adv.","d":"more and more","c":"越來越","s":"Robots are increasingly common in restaurants, and some young children have never ordered food from a person.","t":"機器人在餐廳裡越來越常見,有些小孩甚至從來沒有向真人點過餐。"},{"w":"largely","p":"adv.","d":"mostly; to a great degree","c":"主要地;大部分地","s":"The factory is now largely run by robots, but a small team of engineers works there day and night.","t":"這間工廠現在主要由機器人運作,但有一小組工程師日夜在那裡工作。"},{"w":"merely","p":"adv.","d":"only; nothing more than","c":"僅僅;只不過","s":"The robot is merely a tool, so the people who use it must take responsibility for what it does.","t":"機器人只不過是一個工具,所以使用它的人必須為它所做的事負責。"},{"w":"partially","p":"adv.","d":"not completely; partly","c":"部分地","s":"The new system is only partially automated, so workers still need to check every order before it leaves.","t":"新系統只有部分自動化,所以工人仍然需要在每筆訂單出貨前檢查。"},{"w":"seldom","p":"adv.","d":"not often; rarely","c":"很少;不常","s":"The robot seldom makes mistakes, but when it does, they can be expensive, so humans still check its work.","t":"這台機器人很少犯錯,但一旦犯錯就可能代價高昂,所以人類仍然會檢查它的工作。"},{"w":"undoubtedly","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"無疑地","s":"Robots will undoubtedly change the way we work, but nobody knows exactly which jobs will disappear first.","t":"機器人無疑會改變我們的工作方式,但沒有人確切知道哪些工作會最先消失。"},{"w":"hitherto","p":"adv.","d":"until now; until a particular time","c":"迄今;到目前為止","s":"The robot reached places that had hitherto been impossible to explore, and it sent back amazing pictures from the cave.","t":"這台機器人抵達了迄今無法探索的地方,並從洞穴傳回了驚人的照片。"},{"w":"thus","p":"adv.","d":"as a result; therefore","c":"因此","s":"The robot works all night without breaks, and thus the factory can produce far more goods each day.","t":"機器人整夜工作不休息,因此工廠每天能生產多得多的商品。"},{"w":"henceforth","p":"adv.","d":"from this time on","c":"從今以後","s":"The company announced that henceforth all deliveries in the city centre would be made by robots, so drivers were moved to other areas.","t":"公司宣布從今以後市中心的所有配送都將由機器人完成,所以司機被調到其他地區。"},{"w":"roughly","p":"adv.","d":"about; approximately","c":"大約","s":"roughly half of the jobs in the warehouse are now done by robots, but the company still employs about three hundred people.","t":"倉庫裡大約一半的工作現在由機器人完成,但公司仍然僱用約三百人。"},{"w":"swiftly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly","c":"迅速地","s":"The rescue robot moved swiftly through the smoke, and it found the trapped family within minutes.","t":"救援機器人在煙霧中迅速地移動,並在幾分鐘內找到了受困的一家人。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"wear and tear","p":"n.phr.","d":"damage that happens through normal use over time","c":"(正常使用造成的)磨損","s":"After five years of daily use, the robot showed signs of wear and tear, so the company replaced its wheels and joints.","t":"經過五年的每日使用,這台機器人出現了磨損的跡象,所以公司更換了它的輪子和關節。"},{"w":"around the clock","p":"phr.","d":"all day and all night without stopping","c":"日以繼夜;全天候","s":"Robots in the warehouse work around the clock, so customers can receive their orders even on public holidays.","t":"倉庫裡的機器人全天候工作,所以顧客即使在國定假日也能收到訂單。"},{"w":"put to the test","p":"v.phr.","d":"to check how good something is by using it in a hard situation","c":"接受考驗;測試","s":"The rescue robot was put to the test after the earthquake, and it found three people under the broken building.","t":"救援機器人在地震後接受了考驗,它在倒塌的建築下找到了三個人。"},{"w":"come into play","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start to have an effect","c":"開始發揮作用","s":"Human judgement must come into play when the robot faces a new situation, because it only knows what it has learned.","t":"當機器人面臨新情況時,人類的判斷力就必須開始發揮作用,因為它只知道它學過的東西。"},{"w":"at the push of a button","p":"phr.","d":"very easily, by just pressing a button","c":"一按按鈕就;輕而易舉地","s":"You can start the robot vacuum at the push of a button, and it will clean the whole flat by itself.","t":"你一按按鈕就能啟動掃地機器人,它會自己打掃整間公寓。"},{"w":"phase in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to introduce something gradually","c":"逐步採用;分階段實施","s":"The city plans to phase in robot buses over five years, so drivers will have time to train for new jobs.","t":"市政府計畫在五年內逐步引進機器人公車,這樣司機就有時間接受新工作的訓練。"},{"w":"step in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become involved to help or stop a problem","c":"介入;出面","s":"If the robot cannot answer a customer's question, a staff member will step in and help them right away.","t":"如果機器人無法回答顧客的問題,員工會介入並立即協助他們。"},{"w":"keep an eye on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to watch something carefully","c":"留意;看管","s":"A supervisor must keep an eye on the robots during the night shift, because a small problem can quickly become serious.","t":"夜班期間必須有一位主管留意機器人,因為小問題很快就可能變得嚴重。"},{"w":"level the playing field","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a situation fair for everyone","c":"創造公平的競爭環境","s":"Video technology helps level the playing field in sport, because every team gets the same fair decisions.","t":"影像科技有助於在運動中創造公平的競爭環境,因為每支隊伍都得到同樣公正的判決。"},{"w":"the benefit of the doubt","p":"n.phr.","d":"believing someone when you are not completely sure","c":"(在不確定時)姑且相信","s":"Human umpires sometimes gave popular players the benefit of the doubt, but the robot treats everyone exactly the same.","t":"人類裁判有時會對受歡迎的球員姑且相信,但機器人對每個人都一視同仁。"},{"w":"call the shots","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the person who makes the important decisions","c":"發號施令;做主","s":"Robots may do the work, but humans still call the shots, so we decide what the machines should and should not do.","t":"機器人也許負責做事,但人類仍然發號施令,所以由我們決定機器該做和不該做什麼。"},{"w":"at a standstill","p":"phr.","d":"not moving or making any progress","c":"陷入停頓;停滯","s":"The whole warehouse was at a standstill after the computer crashed, so hundreds of parcels were delivered late.","t":"電腦當機後整個倉庫陷入停頓,所以數百個包裹延遲送達。"},{"w":"up and running","p":"adj.phr.","d":"working properly after being set up or repaired","c":"開始運作;正常運轉","s":"The technicians got the robots up and running again within an hour, so the factory lost very little time.","t":"技術人員在一小時內就讓機器人重新正常運轉,所以工廠幾乎沒有損失時間。"},{"w":"second nature","p":"n.phr.","d":"something you do easily without thinking","c":"第二天性;習以為常","s":"Using voice commands has become second nature for my children, so they talk to the smart speaker like a friend.","t":"使用語音指令對我的孩子們來說已經成為第二天性,所以他們像跟朋友一樣和智慧音箱說話。"},{"w":"move with the times","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change your ideas or methods as the world changes","c":"與時俱進","s":"Older shop owners must move with the times, or they may lose customers to stores that use modern technology.","t":"年長的店主必須與時俱進,否則他們可能會把顧客輸給使用現代科技的商店。"},{"w":"pave the way for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make it possible for something to happen later","c":"為…鋪路","s":"Early factory robots helped pave the way for today's home robots, because they proved that machines could work safely.","t":"早期的工廠機器人幫忙為今日的家用機器人鋪路,因為它們證明了機器可以安全地工作。"},{"w":"here to stay","p":"adj.phr.","d":"accepted and likely to continue for a long time","c":"會一直存在;不會消失","s":"Some people still dislike robot waiters, but most experts agree that this technology is here to stay.","t":"有些人仍然不喜歡機器人服務生,但大多數專家都同意這項技術會一直存在。"},{"w":"by hand","p":"phr.","d":"using your hands, not a machine","c":"用手;手工","s":"My grandmother still washes her clothes by hand, although we bought her a washing machine last year.","t":"我奶奶仍然用手洗衣服,雖然我們去年買了一台洗衣機給她。"},{"w":"a close call","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation where something bad almost happened","c":"千鈞一髮;險些出事","s":"It was a close call when the robot arm nearly hit a worker, so the factory moved the safety line further back.","t":"當機器手臂差點撞到一名工人時真是千鈞一髮,所以工廠把安全線往後移。"},{"w":"on the line","p":"phr.","d":"at risk of being lost or damaged","c":"岌岌可危;面臨風險","s":"Thousands of jobs are on the line because of the new robots, so the union is meeting the company next week.","t":"因為新機器人,數千個工作岌岌可危,所以工會下週將和公司會面。"}]}];
